54199,NAP-300-AU23.5PAB,bhavesh,Aurum Gold Leaf 23.5 Kt Patent (Book) Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Aurum Gold Leaf 23.5 Kt Patent (Book) Made in USA by Natural Pigments,0.010,44.500,44.500,,"Aurum Gold Leaf 23.5 Kt Patent (Book)<bR><br> <EOL><b>About Aurum Gold Leaf</b><BR> <EOL>Aurum gold leaf is our own brand of high quality leaf product. This leaf is manufactured specifically in the colors and weights that are standard in the industry. This leaf is produced using the latest technology and respected traditions of the gold beating craft.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL>Patent gold leaf, also referred to transfer gold leaf, is gold leaf mounted on a special tissue paper by a pressure process. A book of patent gold leaf is assembled by placing each unit of gold leaf between sheets of thin rouged paper. The gilder can then remove one leaf at a time without disturbing the remaining leaves.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL>Our gold leaf is made in the standard European size of 80 x 80 mm (3.15 x 3.15 inches) and is available in units called ""books,"" each book containing 25 leaves. For volume discounts order one or more boxes of gold leaf.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>Patent 23.5 karat gold leaf, Average weight: 16 grams per 1,000 leaves<br> <EOL>Pack of 20 books, each book contains 25, 500 leaves total.</b> <EOL>",,0,2,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,57.630,,Thursday 11 November 2010 06:01:30 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,44.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54200,NAP-300-AU23.5PAP,bhavesh,Aurum Gold Leaf 23.5 Kt Patent (Pack) Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Aurum Gold Leaf 23.5 Kt Patent (Pack) Made in USA by Natural Pigments,0.040,712,712,,"Aurum Gold Leaf 23.5 Kt Patent (Pack)<bR><br> <EOL><b>About Aurum Gold Leaf</b><BR> <EOL>Aurum gold leaf is our own brand of high quality leaf product. This leaf is manufactured specifically in the colors and weights that are standard in the industry. This leaf is produced using the latest technology and respected traditions of the gold beating craft.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL>Patent gold leaf, also referred to transfer gold leaf, is gold leaf mounted on a special tissue paper by a pressure process. A book of patent gold leaf is assembled by placing each unit of gold leaf between sheets of thin rouged paper. The gilder can then remove one leaf at a time without disturbing the remaining leaves.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL>Our gold leaf is made in the standard European size of 80 x 80 mm (3.15 x 3.15 inches) and is available in units called ""books,"" each book containing 25 leaves.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>Patent 23.5 karat gold leaf, Average weight: 16 grams per 1,000 leaves<br> <EOL>Pack of 20 books, each book contains 25, 500 leaves total.</b> <EOL>",,0,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,876.890,,Thursday 11 November 2010 06:06:24 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,712,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54423,NAP-370-RBTUBE,bhavesh2,Aurum Reed Breathing Tube: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Aurum Reed Breathing Tube by Natural Pigments,0.010,4.450,4.450,,"Aurum Reed Breathing Tube<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b> About Aurum Reed Breathing Tube</b><BR> <EOL>Used to moisten the surfaces of gilding bases, containing hide glue or gelatin, immediately before laying gold leaf. The moisture from your breath ""activates"" the glue allowing metal leaf, such as gold, silver or palladium, to adhere to the gilding base. A reed tube controls condensation and absorbs excess moisture that accumulates as you breathe through it, preventing drops of moisture from forming and falling on your working surface. If drops fall on the base, unnoticed, the gold and base will come apart during burnishing. If they fall on the gold, subsequent layers will come off when applied. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL><b>How To Use</b><br> <EOL>To use simply aim the tube at the area where metal leaf is to be laid, about 3 to 5 cm (1 to 2 inches) above the surface, and exhale strongly through the tube, allowing your breath to cover the entire area to be immediately covered. When exhaling, blow from the throat, do not puff from the mouth, as you want warm moisture to form on the base. Exhale slowly and evenly, about the length of a sigh, two or three times. <EOL>",,1000000,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,57728,Painting and Painting Accessories/Raw Materials/Pigments,,6.050,,Friday 12 November 2010 07:41:03 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,4.450,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54208,NAP-300-AUSLVSFB,bhavesh,"Aurum Silver Leaf (Book): 95 x 95 mm, Book of 25 leaves, Made in USA by Natural Pigments","Aurum Silver Leaf (Book): 95 x 95 mm, Book of 25 leaves",0.010,12.350,12.350,,"Aurum Silver Leaf (Book): 95 x 95 mm, Book of 25 leaves<bR><br> <EOL><b>About Aurum Silver</b><BR> <EOL>Aurum genuine pure, heavy silver leaf is produced using the latest technology and respected traditions of the Italian gold beating craft.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL>A book of loose silver leaf is assembled by placing each unit of silver leaf between sheets of thin rouged paper. The gilder can then remove one leaf at a time without disturbing the remaining leaves. It is removed from the book with a gilder's tip, a flat natural hair brush. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Aurum silver leaf 95 x 95 mm (3-3/4 x 3-3/4 inches)and is available in units called ""books,"" each book containing 25 leaves. For volume discounts order one or more ""packs"" of silver leaf; each pack contains 20 books or 500 leaves. <EOL>",,0,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,16.520,,Thursday 11 November 2010 06:21:04 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,12.350,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54213,NAP-300-AUSLVSFP,bhavesh,"Aurum Silver Leaf (Pack): 95 x 95 mm, Pack of 20 Books or 500 Leaves, Made in USA by Natural Pigments","Aurum Silver Leaf (Pack): 95 x 95 mm, Pack of 20 Books or 500 Leaves",0.030,191.250,191.250,,"Aurum 95 x 95 mm (3-3/4 x 3-3/4 inches) book of 25 leaves, pack contains 20 books or 500 leaves <bR><br> <EOL>Aurum genuine pure, heavy silver leaf is produced using the latest technology and respected traditions of silver beating craft.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL>A book of loose silver leaf is assembled by placing each unit of silver leaf between sheets of thin rouged paper. The gilder can then remove one leaf at a time without disturbing the remaining leaves. It is removed from the book with a gilder's tip, a flat natural hair brush. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Loose, heavy silver leaf<br> <EOL>Average weight: 33 grams per 1,000 leaves",,0,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,235.550,,Thursday 11 November 2010 06:27:56 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,191.250,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55300,NAP-530-36510,bhavesh,Balsam Essential Oil Medium 100 ml: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Balsam Essential Oil Medium 100 ml: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,0.250,25.500,25.500,,"Balsam Essential Oil Medium 4 fl oz (118 ml)<BR><br> <EOL><b>About Balsam Essential</b><Br> <EOL>Rublev Colours Balsam Essential Oil Medium is composed of Canada balsam, pale bodied linseed oil and spike oil. Add to oil paint for enamel-like effects (gloss and greater color saturation), to achieve glow in glazes and to facilitate fusion of the colors and brushstrokes.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>How to Use</b><br> <EOL>Add a small amount of Balsam Essential Oil Medium to your paint to make it brush out more eas­ily, adhere bet­ter to pre­vi­ous layers, and dry more quickly. Balsam Essential Oil Medium can be thinned with spike oil or turpentine. Mixed directly into paint on the palette, it gives colors a flowing consistency yet dries to a satin to gloss finish, depending upon the amount used. Balsam Essential Oil Medium smells wonderful.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL>Rublev Colours Balsam Essential Oil Medium is an excellent substitute for Ralph Mayer’s glazing medium described in his handbook, The Artist's Handbook of Materials and Techniques, which is a medium composed of stand oil, damar varnish, and turpentine.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Ingredients</b> <EOL>Balsam Essential Oil Medium is a 44% weight to volume solution of Canada balsam in bodied linseed oil and lavender spike oil (44% w/v resin solution). Canada balsam is a turpentine made from the resin of the balsam fir tree (Abies balsamea) that grows in boreal North America. The resin, dissolved in essential oils, is a viscous, sticky, yellowish liquid that becomes a transparent yellowish mass when the essential oils evaporate. Canada balsam becomes amorphous solid upon drying. Since it does not crystallize with age, its optical properties do not deteriorate. This volatile resin improves adhe­sion from one paint layer to another and imparts a silky smooth qual­ity to paint. Canada bal­sam is clearer and faster-drying than Venice turpen­tine.<br><br> <EOL>Balsam Essential Oil Medium contains the palest bodied linseed oil to provide greater leveling and flow out and better drying properties.<br><br> <EOL>Balsam Essential Oil Medium contains lavender spike oil. Spike oil is an essential oil obtained by distillation of the flower spikes of the herb Lavandula latifolia or other related species. It is a solvent commonly used in oil painting by European old masters. For instance, Francisco Pacheco mentions the use of spike oil in his book Arte de la pintura (1649). It is composed primarily of linalool (51%) and linalyl acetate (35%) but also includes other components found in turpentine, such as α-pinene, limonene, 1,8-cineole, cis- and trans-ocimene, 3-octanone, camphor, caryophyllene, terpinen-4-ol and lavendulyl acetate. <EOL> <EOL> <EOL>",,999996,5,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8727,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Vehicles & Mediums/Oils,,22.990,,Wednesday 17 November 2010 08:53:45 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,19.130,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54825,NAP-510-11BRT5K,bhavesh,Barite 5 Kg (11 lbs) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Barite 5 Kg (11 lbs) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,11,80,80,,"Barite 5 Kg (11 lbs) Bag<BR><br> <EOL><b>About Barite</b><br> <EOL>Rublev Barite is made using the highest quality white, natural barium sulfate ore. Its unique properties of fine grind (3 micron median particle size), high specific gravity (4.4) and chemical inertness make it ideal for grounds, to make white paint and as paint filler.",,999995,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8680,"Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Grounds/Silica, Talc, Barite with Bags",,77.060,,Monday 15 November 2010 06:55:35 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,60,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54039,NAP-920-BP1114,bhavesh2,"Baroque Artist Birch Panel: 11"" x 14"", Made in USA by Natural Pigments",Baroque Artist Birch Panel: 11" x 14" by Natural Pigments,0.500,14.350,14.350,,"Baroque Artist Birch Panel: 11"" x 14""<br><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><BR> <EOL>* Overall Dimensions: 11 x 14 x 0.875 in. (28 x 35 x 2.2 cm)<br> <EOL>* Panel Material: Baltic Birch plywood<br> <EOL>* Finish: None<br> <EOL>* Braces: Birch<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Baroque Artist Panels</b><BR> <EOL>Baroque Artist Panels can make your work easier, saving you time and money from building your own panels. Built to handle various mediums, their lightweight construction eliminates excessive weight and allows for easy storage and transport. These panels are expressly made for use by professional painters, but are ideal for student work because of their low price.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL>Baroque Artist Panels' fine finished surfaces are of Birch, specially selected for its density and hardness, which is sanded to a satin smooth finish providing an excellent surface for drawing, painting, pastel and multimedia work. These Birch panels are different from other boards. They are not made from a single piece of wood, but from high quality Baltic Birch plywood. The structure of Birch plywood consists of laminated sheets of wood, so it avoids deformation and warping common with solid wood panels, and it is lighter in weight. The face of Baroque Artist Panels are made from hand-selected, 5 mm (3/16 in.) thick plywood consisting of two-plies of clear (no knots or imperfections) Birch. The panels are cut, chamfers are made on all four edges of the face and entirely machine-sanded for a smooth final finish. The bare finish of Baroque Artist Panels are ready for sizing and applying gesso or paint primer. Baroque Artist Panels are braced on the back with 0.75 by 1.125 in. (20 x 28 mm) solid wood to prevent deformation and warping.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>Directions</b><Br> <EOL>Clean surface with rag or paper towel to remove any dust. Apply gesso, acrylic dispersion primer or oil primer directly to surface. If surface is too absorbent, apply a light coat of Sealing Varnish before applying gesso, acrylic dispersion primer or oil primer. To improve adhesion, it is best to lightly sand the panel face before applying the primer. For best results, apply Sealing Varnish or paint to edges and back to reduce moisture absorption. <EOL>",,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,50263,Furniture for Artists/Lamps and Lighting,,19.040,,Wednesday 10 November 2010 06:02:14 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,14.350,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54040,NAP-920-BP1216,bhavesh2,"Baroque Artist Birch Panel: 12"" x 16"", Made in USA by Natural Pigments",Baroque Artist Birch Panel: 12" x 16" by Natural Pigments,0.500,15,15,,"Baroque Artist Birch Panel: 12"" x 16""<br><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><BR> <EOL>* Overall Dimensions: 12 x 16 x 0.875 in. (30 x 40 x 2.2 cm)<br> <EOL>* Panel Material: Baltic Birch plywood<br> <EOL>* Finish: None<br> <EOL>* Braces: Birch<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Baroque Artist Panels</b><BR> <EOL>Baroque Artist Panels can make your work easier, saving you time and money from building your own panels. Built to handle various mediums, their lightweight construction eliminates excessive weight and allows for easy storage and transport. These panels are expressly made for use by professional painters, but are ideal for student work because of their low price.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL>Baroque Artist Panels' fine finished surfaces are of Birch, specially selected for its density and hardness, which is sanded to a satin smooth finish providing an excellent surface for drawing, painting, pastel and multimedia work. These Birch panels are different from other boards. They are not made from a single piece of wood, but from high quality Baltic Birch plywood. The structure of Birch plywood consists of laminated sheets of wood, so it avoids deformation and warping common with solid wood panels, and it is lighter in weight. The face of Baroque Artist Panels are made from hand-selected, 5 mm (3/16 in.) thick plywood consisting of two-plies of clear (no knots or imperfections) Birch. The panels are cut, chamfers are made on all four edges of the face and entirely machine-sanded for a smooth final finish. The bare finish of Baroque Artist Panels are ready for sizing and applying gesso or paint primer. Baroque Artist Panels are braced on the back with 0.75 by 1.125 in. (20 x 28 mm) solid wood to prevent deformation and warping.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>Directions</b><Br> <EOL>Clean surface with rag or paper towel to remove any dust. Apply gesso, acrylic dispersion primer or oil primer directly to surface. If surface is too absorbent, apply a light coat of Sealing Varnish before applying gesso, acrylic dispersion primer or oil primer. To improve adhesion, it is best to lightly sand the panel face before applying the primer. For best results, apply Sealing Varnish or paint to edges and back to reduce moisture absorption. <EOL>",,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8574,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Artist Birch Panels,,19.910,,Wednesday 10 November 2010 06:05:21 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,15,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
