oated liberally with linseed or tung oil. The cellulose fibers of hardboard can then be expected to suffer the same degradation as cellulosic linen, cotton or paper fibers coming in contact with an acidic drying oil. The tempering process may well yield a better construction product, but can only degrade the board from an artist's point of view. For this reason, we use only untempered or Standard Hardboard made of aspen and other hardwoods to make Natural Pigments Gesso Panels. <EOL><br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>The Real Thing--Traditional Gesso</b><br> <EOL>Several coats of gesso are applied to the face of the panel and sanded to a smooth satin finish. The traditional gesso is made using only the highest quality calcite (calcium carbonate) and collagen glue (rabbit skin grade)--this is not acrylic dispersion primer, but a chalk ground based on traditional and centuries-old formulas. <EOL>",,0,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8575,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Hardboard Gesso Panels,,15.140,,Wednesday 10 November 2010 06:56:28 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,11,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
