53496,KOL-702-5234004,ariel2,Kolibri Mop Brush # 8 (Made in Germany),Kolibri Mop Brush # 8 (Made in Germany),0.050,8.650,8.650,,Kolibri Mop Brush # 8<br><Br> <EOL><b>Specifications:</b><Br> <EOL>* Brush Type: Mop<br> <EOL>* Hair Type: Goat and pony mixture<bR> <EOL>* Ferrule: Nickel-plated brass<br> <EOL>* Size: 8<br> <EOL>* Hair Width: 3.18 cm (1.25 in.)<br> <EOL>* Hair Length: 3.18 cm (1.25 in.)<br> <EOL>* Handle Length including ferrule: 18.4 cm (7.25 in.)<br><br> <EOL><b>About Mop Brush</b><BR> <EOL>This mop brush is made from a mixture of pony and goat hair that is 1.9 cm (0.75 inch) out of the ferrule. The brush has a seamless nickel-plated brass ferrule on silver polished wood handle. <EOL><br><bR> <EOL><b>Painting</b><br> <EOL>The mop brush is ideal for washes and broad applications of paint. The large head of soft natural hair holds an immense volume of paint that can easily be drawn across paper or gesso surface. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL><b>Gilding</b><Br> <EOL>This brush makes an ideal duster for gilding to remove pieces of gold leaf or to dust off the gilding base before applying the leaf. The soft hairs of this brush will not scratch the gilding base or the gold once applied.,,0,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,9.820,,Wednesday 03 November 2010 06:51:49 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,280,,4.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53531,KOL-704-1210,ariel2,Kolibri Natural Bristle Flat Brush # 10 (Made in Germany),Kolibri Natural Bristle Flat Brush # 10 (Made in Germany),0.060,5.900,5.900,,"Kolibri Natural Bristle Flat Brush (Size 10)<br> <EOL><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><br> <EOL>* Suitable For Oil, Acrylics, Fresco and Encaustic<br> <EOL>* Brush Style: Flat<br> <EOL>* Hair Type: Natural Chungking Bristle<br> <EOL>* Ferrule: Nickel-plated brass<br> <EOL>* Size: 10<br> <EOL>* Hair Width: 9.5 mm (3/8 in.)<br> <EOL>* Hair Length: 16.0 mm (5/8 in.)<br> <EOL>* Handle Length: 26.7 cm (10.5 in.)<br> <EOL><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Kolibri Bristle Brushes</b><br> <EOL>Kolibri bristle brushes are handmade in Germany by Feurer & Sohn -- one of the oldest brush manufacturers in Germany (established 1898). These natural bristle brushes are made from the finest Chungking (or Chongqing) unbleached hog bristles. <br><br> <EOL> <EOL> <EOL><b>Natural Bristles</b><br> <EOL>Natural hog bristles differ from other hairs due to the V-shaped split or ""flag"" at the tip of the bristles. The flag allows you to load more paint on the brush and provides smoother brushing. What makes Chungking bristles unlike any other natural bristles is that they have a natural curve. Each brush is hand crafted with ""interlocked"" bristles, meaning the natural curves of the bristles are positioned inward toward the ferrule, which gives the brush a natural resistance to fraying and spreads medium to thick paints smoothly and evenly.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL>A selection of pure hog bristle brushes is recommended for oil and acrylic painting, and is a far less expensive alternative to good quality softer hairs. Natural bristle brushes also work well in fresco and encaustic painting.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Nickel-Plated Brass Ferrules</b><br> <EOL>The ferrule of each Kolibri bristle brush receives two deep crimps. Deep crimping compresses the walls of the ferrule into the wooden handle, creating a mechanical lock that securely fastens the ferrule to the handle.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Hardwood Handles</b><br> <EOL>The long ivory-colored polished handles are made of hardwood and are lacquer finished for long life. Only the best brush handles are dipped. They are made by lowering the handles first in primer, then twice in colored lacquer and finally in varnish -- a total of four coats -- for a lustrous durable finish. For ease of handling in both a pencil or palm grip, the hardwood handles are over 25 cm (10 in.) from the ferrule to handle end. The long handle permits you to stand back from the painting while working to have a better view of your subject.<br><br> <EOL>",,0,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,6.700,,Wednesday 03 November 2010 08:11:11 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,280,,3.070,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
