53529,KOL-704-1208,ariel2,Kolibri Natural Bristle Flat Brush # 8 (Made in Germany),Kolibri Natural Bristle Flat Brush # 8 (Made in Germany),0.050,5.850,5.850,,"Kolibri Natural Bristle Flat Brush (Size 8)<br> <EOL><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><br> <EOL>* Suitable For Oil, Acrylics, Fresco and Encaustic<br> <EOL>* Brush Style: Flat<br> <EOL>* Hair Type: Natural Chungking Bristle<br> <EOL>* Ferrule: Nickel-plated brass<br> <EOL>* Size: 8<br> <EOL>* Hair Width: 9.5 mm (3/8 in.)<br> <EOL>* Hair Length: 16.0 mm (5/8 in.)<br> <EOL>* Handle Length: 26.7 cm (10.5 in.)<br> <EOL><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Kolibri Bristle Brushes</b><br> <EOL>Kolibri bristle brushes are handmade in Germany by Feurer & Sohn -- one of the oldest brush manufacturers in Germany (established 1898). These natural bristle brushes are made from the finest Chungking (or Chongqing) unbleached hog bristles. <br><br> <EOL> <EOL> <EOL><b>Natural Bristles</b><br> <EOL>Natural hog bristles differ from other hairs due to the V-shaped split or ""flag"" at the tip of the bristles. The flag allows you to load more paint on the brush and provides smoother brushing. What makes Chungking bristles unlike any other natural bristles is that they have a natural curve. Each brush is hand crafted with ""interlocked"" bristles, meaning the natural curves of the bristles are positioned inward toward the ferrule, which gives the brush a natural resistance to fraying and spreads medium to thick paints smoothly and evenly.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL>A selection of pure hog bristle brushes is recommended for oil and acrylic painting, and is a far less expensive alternative to good quality softer hairs. Natural bristle brushes also work well in fresco and encaustic painting.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Nickel-Plated Brass Ferrules</b><br> <EOL>The ferrule of each Kolibri bristle brush receives two deep crimps. Deep crimping compresses the walls of the ferrule into the wooden handle, creating a mechanical lock that securely fastens the ferrule to the handle.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Hardwood Handles</b><br> <EOL>The long ivory-colored polished handles are made of hardwood and are lacquer finished for long life. Only the best brush handles are dipped. They are made by lowering the handles first in primer, then twice in colored lacquer and finally in varnish -- a total of four coats -- for a lustrous durable finish. For ease of handling in both a pencil or palm grip, the hardwood handles are over 25 cm (10 in.) from the ferrule to handle end. The long handle permits you to stand back from the painting while working to have a better view of your subject.<br><br> <EOL>",,0,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,6.640,,Wednesday 03 November 2010 08:06:53 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,280,,3.040,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53252,KOL-702-33300,ariel2,Kolibri Red Sable Detail Brush # 0 (Made in Germany),Kolibri Red Sable Detail Brush # 0 (Made in Germany),0.010,6,6,,"Red Sable Detail Brush (Size 0)<br> <EOL><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><br> <EOL>* Suitable For Watercolor, Acrylics and Tempera<br> <EOL>* Brush Style: Round<br> <EOL>* Hair Type: Red Sable<br> <EOL>* Ferrule: Silver-plated brass<br> <EOL>* Size: 0<br> <EOL>* Hair Width: 1.5 mm (1/16 in.)<br> <EOL>* Hair Length: 7 mm (1/4 in.)<br> <EOL>* Handle Length: 14.5 cm (5.5 in.)<br> <EOL><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Kolibri Brushes</b><br> <EOL>Kolibri brushes are handmade in Germany by Feurer & Sohn, one of the oldest brush manufacturers in Germany (established 1898). They are made by dedicated brush makers, using the highest quality hair obtained in Russia.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL>Kolibri Red Sable Detail brushes are designed for painting the sharpest details with fluid paint. They are made from the tail hair of the weasel (Mustela nivalis) found in northern China. <EOL><br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Silver-Plated Brass Ferrules</b><br> <EOL>The ferrule of each Kolibri Red Sable Detail brush receives two deep crimps. Deep crimping compresses the walls of the ferrule into the wooden handle, creating a mechanical lock that securely fastens the ferrule to the handle. <br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Hardwood Handles</b><br> <EOL>The short red polished handles are made of hardwood and are lacquer finished for long life. Only the best brush handles are dipped. They are made by lowering the handles first in primer, then twice in colored lacquer and finally in varnish -- a total of four coats -- for a lustrous durable finish. For ease of handling in a pencil grip, the hardwood handles are 14 cm (5.5 in.) from the ferrule to handle end. The handle's triangular shape provides a comfortable grip that is secure while working to allow you to make the finest details. The triangular shape also prevents the brush from rolling off tables and work surfaces.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>More About Sable Hair</b><br> <EOL>When you see the term ""sable"" it is not really from sable at all, but comes from the tail of a species that is a member of the weasel family (Mustela) found in many areas of the world. The sable (Martes zibellina) is a species of marten. Originally, the name ""weasel"" was applied to one species of the genus, the European Least Weasel (Mustela nivalis). In technical discourse, the term ""weasel"" can refer to any member of the genus, or to the genus as a whole. Of the 16 extant species currently classified in the genus Mustela, ten have ""weasel"" in their common name. Among those that do not are the stoat or ermine, the two species of mink, and the polecats or ferrets. Weasel hair is generally conceded to be the second best hair for oil and watercolor painting brushes due to its strength, spring and ability to retain its shape. The finest hair is Kolinksy sable, which comes from another species of weasel found in Siberia. Only weasel tail hair from northern Asia is long and fine enough to be suitable for brush making. The hair can be distinguished by their reddish brown color whereas Kolinsky is golden brown and longer than weasel hair. Our sable brushes are made from weasels found in northern China and hold a very fine point or edge, is a professional grade of hair, and, if properly cared for, will last for many years. Other manufacturers may make their brushes from a mixture of weasel and ox hair, commonly used to manufacture most medium and low-priced red sable brushes.",,0,3,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,7.420,,Monday 01 November 2010 06:25:18 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,280,,6,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
