53373,KOL-701-1306,ariel2,Kolinsky Flat Brush # 6 (Made in Russia),Kolinsky Flat Brush # 6 (Made in Russia),0.040,19.160,19.160,,"Kolinsky Flat Brush (Size # 6)<br><br> <EOL> <EOL>We make no pretense... these are not beautiful brushes, but they work wonderfully with most water-based and oil-based paint. We located a craftsman in Russia who makes brushes for many of the best icon painting workshops and masters. His reputation was among the highest, so we asked him to make brushes for Iconofile.<br><Br> <EOL> <EOL>The fur from the Siberian winter male Kolinsky makes the very best tempera and watercolor brushes because of its unique water-carrying properties. It's extremely soft and supple, yet strong and elastic. Crafted to take advantage of these special qualities, our tempera brushes are made with longer tapered Kolinsky hair, hand-cupped by our expert brushmaker to produce a precise point. A dense hair count and full, tapered belly maximize our brushes' holding power. The hairs are deeply set into the nickel-plated brass ferrules, producing excellent spring and control, and return to a point immediately when raised from the board. For ease of handling in both a pencil or palm grip, the bare hardwood handles are made longer than watercolor yet shorter than oil brush handles -- 26.5 cm (10.5 in.) from brush tip to handle end. <EOL><br><br> <EOL>When you see the term ""Kolinsky Sable"" it is not really from sable at all, but comes from the tail of a species of mink that is a member of the weasel family (Mustela siberica) found in Siberia and northeastern China. The very best Kolinsky brushes are made with hair from the tail of the male animal's winter coat. Although Kolinskies are also found in northern China and northern Japan, the best hair is from animals in the northern-most parts of Siberia. Kolinskies must be trapped in the wild as opposed to raised on fur farms as mink are today. Kolinsky hair is generally conceded to be the best material for oil and watercolor brushes due to its strength, spring and ability to retain its shape (sometimes called ""snap""). It holds a very fine point or edge. This is considered a professional grade of hair, and if properly cared for, Kolinsky will last for many years. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>The Natural Pigments Kolinsky Series brushes are made in Russia and sized with the European system which begins with 0. An English size 6 watercolor round is equivalent to a European size 7 Natural Pigments brush. <EOL>",,0,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,21.760,,Tuesday 02 November 2010 06:03:50 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,280,,9.960,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
59847,NAP-701-1102,bhavesh2,"Kolinsky Round Brush # 2, Made in USA by Natural Pigments","Kolinsky Round Brush # 2, Made in USA by Natural Pigments",0.020,13.240,13.240,,"Kolinsky Round Brush # 2, Made in USA by Natural Pigments<br><br> <EOL><b> About Kolinsky Round Brush</b><BR> <EOL>We make no pretense... these are not beautiful brushes, but they work wonderfully with most water-based and oil-based paint. We located a craftsman in Russia who makes brushes for many of the best icon painting workshops and masters. His reputation was among the highest, so we asked him to make brushes for Iconofile. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>The fur from the Siberian winter male Kolinsky makes the very best tempera and watercolor brushes because of its unique water-carrying properties. It's extremely soft and supple, yet strong and elastic. Crafted to take advantage of these special qualities, our tempera brushes are made with longer tapered Kolinsky hair, hand-cupped by our expert brushmaker to produce a precise point. A dense hair count and full, tapered belly maximize our brushes' holding power. The hairs are deeply set into the nickel-plated brass ferrules, producing excellent spring and control, and return to a point immediately when raised from the board. For ease of handling in both a pencil or palm grip, the bare hardwood handles are made longer than watercolor yet shorter than oil brush handles -- 26.5 cm (10.5 in.) from brush tip to handle end. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>When you see the term ""Kolinsky Sable"" it is not really from sable at all, but comes from the tail of a species of mink that is a member of the weasel family (Mustela siberica) found in Siberia and northeastern China. The very best Kolinsky brushes are made with hair from the tail of the male animal's winter coat. Although Kolinskies are also found in northern China and northern Japan, the best hair is from animals in the northern-most parts of Siberia. Kolinskies must be trapped in the wild as opposed to raised on fur farms as mink are today. Kolinsky hair is generally conceded to be the best material for oil and watercolor brushes due to its strength, spring and ability to retain its shape (sometimes called ""snap""). It holds a very fine point or edge. This is considered a professional grade of hair, and if properly cared for, Kolinsky will last for many years. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>The Natural Pigments Kolinsky Series brushes are made in Russia and sized with the European system which begins with 0. An English size 6 watercolor round is equivalent to a European size 7 Natural Pigments brush.",,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,47597,Uncategorized/Kolibri Brushes/Kolibri Kolinsky Round Brushes,,17.710,,Saturday 25 December 2010 04:42:47 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,13.240,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
59868,NAP-701-1201,bhavesh2,"Kolinsky Script Brush # 1, Made in USA by Natural Pigments","Kolinsky Kolinsky Script Brush # 1, Made in USA by Natural Pigments",0.020,12.540,12.540,,"Kolinsky Script Brush # 1, Made in USA by Natural Pigments<br><br> <EOL><b> About Kolinsky Script Brush</b><BR> <EOL>Script brushes (also known as ""riggers"" developed by marine painters to paint the lines and rigging of sailing ships) are pointed, narrow brushes with very long hair. The script brush is similar to a round but with much longer hair. Its name is derived from its use in painting scripts and calligraphy. It is ideally suited to this job, because of its ability to make long fine strokes without running out of color. With practice, it can be flexed and lifted to create strokes that taper to fine lines. Script brushes have short handles and round ferrules. The large color carrying capacity is useful for delicate lettering, highlighting, outlining, and long continuous strokes. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Our Kolinsky Script brush has long flowing hair that tapers to a sharp point, and is made with the finest pure Kolinsky hair. The generous belly area holds large amounts of paint--enabling you to make long, continuous lines without recharging the brush. The unvarnished handle of the Kolinsky Script brush is long--about 210 mm (8-1/2"")--not including the ferrule and point. These brushes are responsive, resilient and point beautifully. They are ideal for outlining drawings on gessoed boards, adding details, making highlights on faces, lettering and fine line work of all kinds. Originally developed for water-based paints, such as tempera and watercolor, this brush also works well with diluted oils, alkyds and enamels. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>When you see the term ""Kolinsky Sable"" it is not really from sable at all, but comes from the tail of a species of mink that is a member of the weasel family (Mustela siberica) found in Siberia and northeastern China. The very best Kolinsky brushes are made with hair from the tail of the male animal's winter coat. Although Kolinskies are also found in northern China and northern Japan, the best hair is from animals in the northern-most parts of Siberia. Kolinskies must be trapped in the wild as opposed to raised on fur farms as mink are today. Kolinsky hair is generally conceded to be the best material for oil and watercolor brushes due to its strength, spring and ability to retain its shape (sometimes called ""snap""). It holds a very fine point or edge. This is considered a professional grade of hair, and if properly cared for, Kolinsky will last for many years. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>The Natural Pigments Kolinsky Series brushes are made in Russia and sized with the European system which begins with 0. An English size 6 watercolor round is equivalent to a European size 7 Natural Pigments Kolinsky brush. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL><B>How to Use the Kolinsky Script Brush</b><BR> <EOL>* Load color all the way to the ferrule with paint of ink-like consistency.<BR> <EOL>* When painting, stay up on the tip.  <EOL>* Keep the handle of the brush as close to 90 degrees from your surface as possible. <EOL>* Applying too much pressure will cause hairs to flare out incorrectly. <EOL>* Go slow enough to allow the paint to flow down to the tip.",,999999,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,47598,Uncategorized/Kolibri Brushes/Kolibri Kolinsky Script Brushes,,16.770,,Saturday 25 December 2010 05:27:57 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,12.540,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58583,NAP-540-1308,bhavesh,Lac Water Varnish 237 ml (8 fl oz) Spray Bottle: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Lac Water Varnish 237 ml (8 fl oz) Spray Bottle,0.500,14.950,14.950,,"<br />237 ml (8 fl oz) spray bottle <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Lac Water Varnish is a natural resin varnish that can be used as a fixative on watercolor and tempera painting to isolate painting layers, in glazing techniques and to enhance color saturation. It can also be used to reduce the absorbency of traditional gesso and chalk grounds. It is based on a recipe used by watercolorists of the 19th century. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Can be used in combination with the Crystal Water Varnish to ""fix"" the paint layer before applying Crystal Water Varnish. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Contains natural ingredients. Does not contain organic solvents. Can be thinned with water.<br /><br /> <EOL><b>DIRECTIONS</b><br /> <EOL>Clean brushes with warm water after using this product. If Lac Water Varnish dries on brushes, it can be removed by soaking brushes in household ammonia. To ensure desired results, always make a test piece for your particular application and surface. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Watercolor Paintings:</b> Allow to dry thoroughly (typically overnight, depending on the thickness of paint). <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Tempera Paintings: Allow to dry thoroughly (typically 1-3 days, depending on the thickness of paint). <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Gesso and Chalk Grounds: Allow to dry thoroughly (typically overnight). <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>APPLICATION</b> <EOL>Apply with a wide flat, soft-hair brush or spray on with an atomizer. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Brush Application:</b> Lightly spray onto the surface using the pump spray or with a brush. Wet the surface evenly by gently spreading the varnish over the area to be covered. Brush gently to avoid disturbing the underlying paint. Allow to dry thoroughly before applying another coat. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Spray Application:</b> Spray a fine mist over the surface with an atomizer. Allow to dry thoroughly before applying another coat.",,999997,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,57734,Painting and Painting Accessories/Raw Materials/Varnishes/Acrylic Resin Varnishes,,15.110,,Monday 13 December 2010 07:45:01 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,11.210,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58399,NAP-624-FWCPT25,bhavesh,Large Folding Palette,Large Folding Palette,0.500,9.650,9.650,,"<br />Large Folding Palette for watercolors and other water-based paint features a brush storage space, five brush holders and five mixing areas with 29 color wells. It is 13 x 26 x 2 cm (5 1/4 x 10 1//8 x 0.75 in.) closed and opens to a large 27 x 26 cm (10.5 x 10 1/8 in. ). This durable, heavy plastic palette also features a convenient thumb hole. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>For outdoor painting there are many folding palettes available, but this one is an excellent and cost-effective choice over similarly-designed metal palettes. It can be held like a traditional oil painting palette with the provided thumb hole. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>You can gauge the quality of the palette by the quality of its materials. Some plastic palettes are thinly constructed and flimsy. This injection molded palette is heavier and more durable than many available today. Other plastic palettes can be brittle with unreliable hinges, but not this one. It does not easily stain but can be cleaned with a non-abrasive household stain remover in the event that colors become stubborn to remove.",,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8932,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Tools,,13.010,,Saturday 11 December 2010 08:45:51 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,9.650,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54570,NAP-510-8LWG16,bhavesh,Lead Oil Ground No. 1 (16 oz) 473 ml: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Lead Oil Ground No. 1 (16 oz) 473 ml: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,1,41.250,41.250,,"Lead Oil Ground No. 1 (16 oz) 473 ml <EOL><BR><br> <EOL><b>CAUTION!</b> This product contains lead. Read the Material Safety Data Sheet for more information. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Rublev Lead Oil Ground is a blend of white pigments and linseed oil for a semi-absorbent ground ideal for oil painting. It dries within two days to one week, depending upon local conditions, such as humidity, light and temperature. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>The important characteristics that grounds should have are (1) adhesion, 2) flexibility, 3) penetration control, 4) a type of surface to which upper layers can adhere well, 5) blister and crack resistance, and 6) good application properties. Careful selection of ingredients in an oil ground is essential to impart these qualities to the ground. Ground natural calcite (calcium carbonate) in combination with lead white (basic lead carbonate) and a maximum chalk resistant grade of rutile titanium dioxide have proven to be an excellent choice of pigments in such oil grounds. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Pigments</b><br /> <EOL>We make Rublev Lead Oil Ground #1 using all three white pigments; calcite, lead white and titanium white in just the right proportions to make a film that remains flexible, tough and has some degree of absorbency. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>The dry ground calcite we use in Rublev Lead Oil Ground #1 has a closely controlled particle size distribution. This grade of calcite is designed to provide the lowest possible oil absorption. It offers the desired penetration control with maximum chalk resistance. Calcite aids in forming the type of surface on grounds to which upper layers will adhere easily. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Lead white, and to a lesser degree, ground calcite, have low water absorption properties and hence develop better blister and crack resistance. Furthermore, lead white contributes to more film flexibility. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>The presence of titanium white increases the opacity of this ground and provides a brilliant white surface. We have selected a grade of titanium white that exhibits good hiding and excellent dispersion properties. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Many manufacturers use zinc white to get a brighter white in their white grounds and paint. Zinc oxide is not recommended in oil grounds, since it tends to cause blistering and cracking in oil paint and grounds -- we have not used any zinc in this product. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Vehicle</b><br /> <EOL>After many trials, we have carefully chosen a specific blend of refined and raw linseed oil with heat-bodied linseed oil such that there is a limited penetration of the oil into the canvas or panel to assure good adhesion to this substrate and yet maintain sufficient holdout to establish a good foundation for the upper layers. This blend of linseed oil also provides the best possible leveling properties, so brush and knife marks are minimized.",,999998,4,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8673,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Grounds/Lead Oils,,36.990,,Saturday 13 November 2010 06:02:40 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,30.940,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54573,NAP-510-8LWG32,bhavesh,Lead Oil Ground No. 1 (32 oz) 0.95 L: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Lead Oil Ground No. 1 (32 oz) 0.95 L: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,2,69.750,69.750,,"Lead Oil Ground No. 1 (32 oz) 0.95 L <EOL><BR><br> <EOL><b>CAUTION!</b> This product contains lead. Read the Material Safety Data Sheet for more information. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Rublev Lead Oil Ground is a blend of white pigments and linseed oil for a semi-absorbent ground ideal for oil painting. It dries within two days to one week, depending upon local conditions, such as humidity, light and temperature. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>The important characteristics that grounds should have are (1) adhesion, 2) flexibility, 3) penetration control, 4) a type of surface to which upper layers can adhere well, 5) blister and crack resistance, and 6) good application properties. Careful selection of ingredients in an oil ground is essential to impart these qualities to the ground. Ground natural calcite (calcium carbonate) in combination with lead white (basic lead carbonate) and a maximum chalk resistant grade of rutile titanium dioxide have proven to be an excellent choice of pigments in such oil grounds. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Pigments</b><br /> <EOL>We make Rublev Lead Oil Ground #1 using all three white pigments; calcite, lead white and titanium white in just the right proportions to make a film that remains flexible, tough and has some degree of absorbency. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>The dry ground calcite we use in Rublev Lead Oil Ground #1 has a closely controlled particle size distribution. This grade of calcite is designed to provide the lowest possible oil absorption. It offers the desired penetration control with maximum chalk resistance. Calcite aids in forming the type of surface on grounds to which upper layers will adhere easily. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Lead white, and to a lesser degree, ground calcite, have low water absorption properties and hence develop better blister and crack resistance. Furthermore, lead white contributes to more film flexibility. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>The presence of titanium white increases the opacity of this ground and provides a brilliant white surface. We have selected a grade of titanium white that exhibits good hiding and excellent dispersion properties. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Many manufacturers use zinc white to get a brighter white in their white grounds and paint. Zinc oxide is not recommended in oil grounds, since it tends to cause blistering and cracking in oil paint and grounds -- we have not used any zinc in this product. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Vehicle</b><br /> <EOL>After many trials, we have carefully chosen a specific blend of refined and raw linseed oil with heat-bodied linseed oil such that there is a limited penetration of the oil into the canvas or panel to assure good adhesion to this substrate and yet maintain sufficient holdout to establish a good foundation for the upper layers. This blend of linseed oil also provides the best possible leveling properties, so brush and knife marks are minimized.",,999999,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8673,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Grounds/Lead Oils,,62.330,,Saturday 13 November 2010 06:07:10 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,52.310,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54554,NAP-510-8LWG08,bhavesh,Lead Oil Ground No. 1 (8 oz) 236 ml: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Lead Oil Ground No. 1 (8 oz) 236 ml: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,0.500,27.750,27.750,,"Lead Oil Ground No. 1 (8 oz) 236 ml <EOL><BR><br> <EOL><b>CAUTION!</b> This product contains lead. Read the Material Safety Data Sheet for more information. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Rublev Lead Oil Ground is a blend of white pigments and linseed oil for a semi-absorbent ground ideal for oil painting. It dries within two days to one week, depending upon local conditions, such as humidity, light and temperature. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>The important characteristics that grounds should have are (1) adhesion, 2) flexibility, 3) penetration control, 4) a type of surface to which upper layers can adhere well, 5) blister and crack resistance, and 6) good application properties. Careful selection of ingredients in an oil ground is essential to impart these qualities to the ground. Ground natural calcite (calcium carbonate) in combination with lead white (basic lead carbonate) and a maximum chalk resistant grade of rutile titanium dioxide have proven to be an excellent choice of pigments in such oil grounds. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Pigments</b><br /> <EOL>We make Rublev Lead Oil Ground #1 using all three white pigments; calcite, lead white and titanium white in just the right proportions to make a film that remains flexible, tough and has some degree of absorbency. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>The dry ground calcite we use in Rublev Lead Oil Ground #1 has a closely controlled particle size distribution. This grade of calcite is designed to provide the lowest possible oil absorption. It offers the desired penetration control with maximum chalk resistance. Calcite aids in forming the type of surface on grounds to which upper layers will adhere easily. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Lead white, and to a lesser degree, ground calcite, have low water absorption properties and hence develop better blister and crack resistance. Furthermore, lead white contributes to more film flexibility. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>The presence of titanium white increases the opacity of this ground and provides a brilliant white surface. We have selected a grade of titanium white that exhibits good hiding and excellent dispersion properties. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Many manufacturers use zinc white to get a brighter white in their white grounds and paint. Zinc oxide is not recommended in oil grounds, since it tends to cause blistering and cracking in oil paint and grounds -- we have not used any zinc in this product. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Vehicle</b><br /> <EOL>After many trials, we have carefully chosen a specific blend of refined and raw linseed oil with heat-bodied linseed oil such that there is a limited penetration of the oil into the canvas or panel to assure good adhesion to this substrate and yet maintain sufficient holdout to establish a good foundation for the upper layers. This blend of linseed oil also provides the best possible leveling properties, so brush and knife marks are minimized.",,999997,2,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8673,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Grounds/Lead Oils,,24.980,,Saturday 13 November 2010 05:44:44 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,20.810,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58534,NAP-681-13085,bhavesh2,Leaf and Square Ornamental Tool: 3/8" X 8-1/2",Leaf and Square Ornamental Tool: 3/8" X 8-1/2",0.500,9.400,9.400,,"<B>Leaf and Square Ornamental Tool: 3/8"" X 8-1/2""</b><BR><BR> <EOL><b>About Leaf and Square Ornamental Tool</b><BR> <EOL>The leaf and ornamental tools is ideal for plaster work in small areas, such as inside corners. It is also used in the detailing of ornate shapes and unusual wall surfaces. This tool is perfectly forged and tempered for long life.",,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,57039,"Canvas, Linen and Painting Surfaces/Canvas Rolls/Cotton Canvas Rolls/Acrylic Primed Cotton",,12.680,,Monday 13 December 2010 06:13:59 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,9.400,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55123,NAP-510-35AOS4,bhavesh,Linseed Oil Sampler 2 fl oz 4 Bottles (78 ml): Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Linseed Oil Sampler 2 fl oz 4 Bottles (78 ml) by Natural Pigments,0.100,19.950,19.950,,"Linseed Oil Sampler 2 fl oz 4 Bottles (78 ml) <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>The use of oleoresinous mediums in oil painting can sometimes overly complicate the paint film and lead to disastrous, if not unexpected results. Natural Pigments offers alternatives to oleoresinous mediums for oil painting by offering a sampler of four linseed oil products (2 fluid ounces each) to amend oil colors. Included in the linseed oil sampler are: <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Refined, Aged Oil</b><br /> <EOL>A low acid value linseed oil perfect for diluting mediums, thinning oil colors and making your own oil paint. However, it also has many other uses besides making paint as one artist recently found: He exposed it to sunlight to thicken it with the purpose of making a light-bodied oil. What this did was to make an oil that when mixed with oil colors enabled wash-like glazes that looked almost like watercolor without being smeary or uneven. The oil dried to a very solid film within 1-1/2 days. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Pale Grinders Oil</b><br /> <EOL>Refined, bleached and dewaxed fatty acids linseed oil, is exceptionally light in color and well-suited for grinding colors. Its high acidity gives it excellent pigment wetting properties for making your own oil paint with dry pigments. High acid value oils make it easier to wet pigments difficult to grind, such as lakes and lamp black, and are especially valuable for grinding reactive pigments, such as lead white. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Vacuum-Bodied Oil is a heat-treated and polymerized (thickened) linseed oil. It is made from well-refined linseed oil cooked in vacuum-kettles. Vacuum-bodied oils have lower acid values, better color and yellow less than stand oils obtained by conventional open-kettle cooking and unbodied oils. It provides gloss, flow out and leveling, and non-yellowing characteristics when compared to other stand or bodied oils. Bodied oils form harder films than raw or refined linseed oil. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Epoxide Oil</b><br /> <EOL>A copolymerized linseed oil that is fast drying oil with good chemical and water resistance. Copolymerized linseed oil provides a new vehicle for oil painting that behaves like a drying oil and fast drying resin. The difference is truly astonishing. Use it in place of natural and synthetic resinous mediums to speed up drying and improve film formation. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Warning:</b> Rags or paper towels contaminated with vegetable drying oils, particularly those containing iron oxide pigments are susceptible to spontaneous combustion. To prevent unexpected fires, used rags or paper towels contaminated with oil-based materials should be collected in a closeable, air-tight container. Store water-dampened rags or paper towels in a metal container with an air-tight top. Alternately, washing contaminated rags will remove contaminating materials and eliminate risk.",,999999,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8727,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Vehicles & Mediums/Oils,,18.050,,Tuesday 16 November 2010 08:45:33 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,14.960,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54024,NAP-901-1060AE,rommel,Maped Epure Vinyl Eraser: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Maped Epure Vinyl Eraser: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,0.010,1.250,1.250,, <EOL>* Maped Epure Eraser is a pure white vinyl eraser in an easy-tohold triangular shape that can erase graphite without a trace and soften metalpoint lines.,,999997,8,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,50592,Drawing and Illustration/Erasers,,1.710,,Wednesday 10 November 2010 05:47:28 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,1.250,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55073,NAP-510-33MAS10,ariel2,Mastic (4 oz): Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Mastic (4 oz): Made in USA by Natural Pigments,0.250,43.500,43.500,,"Mastic (4 oz):<BR><br> <EOL><b>About Mastic </b><Br> <EOL>Standard grade of natural resin tapped from trees on the island of Chios, Greece. The small yellow tears are used to make traditional high-grade picture varnishes and painting mediums. This is the most economical way to buy mastic varnish. Mastic can be used as: <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>    * A final picture varnish for oil and tempera paintings.<br> <EOL>    * A medium added to oil paint for transparent glossy glazes.<br> <EOL>    * An ingredient in encaustic medium.<BR> <EOL>    * An ingredient to make egg yolk emulsion that can be thinned with water. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL><b>Mastic Varnish</b><BR> <EOL> <EOL>It is best to prepare damar as a concentrated varnish to make it easier to dilute and use in different recipes. Thinning the concentrated varnish with additional turpentine makes a final picture or a retouch varnish. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL><B>To Make Mastic Concentrate:</b><BR> <EOL>* 1 500 ml (1-pint) container with lid (such as a 1-pint Ball Mason jar)<br> <EOL>* String - the length of about twice the height of the container<br> <EOL>* Unbleached cotton cloth, cheesecloth or similar fabric<br> <EOL>* 100 g mastic tears<br> <EOL>* 300 ml (about 1 cup) pure gum spirits of turpentine<br> <EOL>* Wrap the mastic tears in the cloth to make a small bag and tie the ends together with the string.<br> <EOL><br> <EOL>Pour the turpentine into the 1-pint container. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Place the bag of mastic into the container, leaving one end of the string outside the container. Wet the mastic thoroughly by stirring the bag inside the container. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Close the container. If the lid will not fit because of the string, put the string into the container, on top of the bag, and close it up again. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Stir the contents of the container a couple of times a day. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>After a day or two, when the mastic tears have dissolved, remove the bag and put the lid on the container. If any debris has settled to the bottom, you can decant the damar varnish into another container. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>You now have a fairly concentrated mastic varnish that should be a golden yellow (sometimes slightly turbid) solution. <EOL>",,0,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,49.410,,Tuesday 16 November 2010 07:49:38 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,22.620,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55078,NAP-510-33MAS25,ariel2,Mastic (8.82 oz) 250 g: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Mastic (8.82 oz) 250 g: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,0.550,87,87,,"Mastic (8.82 oz) 250 g<BR><br> <EOL><b>About Mastic </b><Br> <EOL>Standard grade of natural resin tapped from trees on the island of Chios, Greece. The small yellow tears are used to make traditional high-grade picture varnishes and painting mediums. This is the most economical way to buy mastic varnish. Mastic can be used as: <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>    * A final picture varnish for oil and tempera paintings.<br> <EOL>    * A medium added to oil paint for transparent glossy glazes.<br> <EOL>    * An ingredient in encaustic medium.<BR> <EOL>    * An ingredient to make egg yolk emulsion that can be thinned with water. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL><b>Mastic Varnish</b><BR> <EOL> <EOL>It is best to prepare damar as a concentrated varnish to make it easier to dilute and use in different recipes. Thinning the concentrated varnish with additional turpentine makes a final picture or a retouch varnish. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL><B>To Make Mastic Concentrate:</b><BR> <EOL>* 1 1 L (1-Quart) container with lid (such as a 1-quart jar)<br> <EOL>* String - the length of about twice the height of the container<br> <EOL>* Unbleached cotton cloth, cheesecloth or similar fabric<br> <EOL>* 250 g mastic tears<br> <EOL>* 750 ml (about 3 cups) pure gum spirits of turpentine<br> <EOL>* Wrap the mastic tears in the cloth to make a small bag and tie the ends together with the string.<br> <EOL><br> <EOL>Pour the turpentine into the 1-pint container. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Place the bag of mastic into the container, leaving one end of the string outside the container. Wet the mastic thoroughly by stirring the bag inside the container. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Close the container. If the lid will not fit because of the string, put the string into the container, on top of the bag, and close it up again. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Stir the contents of the container a couple of times a day. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>After a day or two, when the mastic tears have dissolved, remove the bag and put the lid on the container. If any debris has settled to the bottom, you can decant the damar varnish into another container. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>You now have a fairly concentrated mastic varnish that should be a golden yellow (sometimes slightly turbid) solution. <EOL>",,0,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,98.820,,Tuesday 16 November 2010 07:54:08 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,45.240,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53939,NAP-900-11TH,ariel2,Metalpoint Holder (Thin) 0.9 mm (0.035 in): Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Metalpoint Holder (Thin) 0.9 mm (0.035 in),0.500,16.950,16.950,,"* Designed for professional use, this auto feed holder features a knurled stainless steel finger grip and reflex cushion point for comfortable drawing control.<br /> <EOL>* The 4 mm long stainless steel sleeve supports the metalpoint and provides drawing accuracy.<br /> <EOL>* Built-in eraser under cap.<br /><br> <EOL> <EOL><b> The following metalpoints can be used with this holder:</b><br /> <EOL>* Silverpoint (Thin, Dead-soft)<br /> <EOL>* Sterling Silverpoint (Thin, Dead-soft)<br /> <EOL>* Sterling Silverpoint (Thin, Half-hard)<br /> <EOL>* Copper point (Thin, Dead-soft)<br /> <EOL>* Brass point (Thin, Dead-soft)",,0,3,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8551,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Points 0.9 mm,,31.130,,Tuesday 09 November 2010 10:22:41 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,16.950,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53942,NAP-900-11WH,ariel2,Metalpoint Holder (Wide) 2 mm (0.08 in): Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Metalpoint Holder (Wide) 2 mm (0.08 in) by Natural Pigments,0.500,15.500,15.500,,"* This is a precision 2mm lead holder with four-way vise grip jaw and spring-loaded point release.<br /> <EOL>* The rugged metal barrel has a knurled finger grip.<br /><br> <EOL><b> The following metalpoints can be used with this holder:</b><br /> <EOL>* Silverpoint (Wide, Dead-soft)<br /> <EOL>* Sterling Silverpoint (Wide, Dead-soft)<br /> <EOL>* Sterling Silverpoint (Wide, Half-hard)<br /> <EOL>* Copper point (Wide, Dead-soft)<br /> <EOL>* Brass point (Wide, Dead-soft)",,0,2,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8577,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Points 2 mm,,20.870,,Tuesday 09 November 2010 10:26:46 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,15.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58531,NAP-681-11167,ariel2,Mixing Board,Mixing Board,0.500,28.500,28.500,,"<B>Mixing Board</b><BR><BR> <EOL><b>About Mixing Board</b><BR> <EOL>The mixing board is made of extra high density, UV stabilized polyethylene. It is durable, lightweight, and easy to clean after mixing plaster. It is not affected by heat and cold, rust, plaster, mortar and water. Dry plaster will not stick to its surface, so clean up is easy. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>The mixing board won't suck the moisture out of your plaster like wooden boards or evaporate the water out like steel boards in hotter temperatures. With a solid flexible, plastic working surface, the mixing board reduces retempering (adding water to dried plaster) and increases plaster board life by as much as 20 to 25 minutes. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>If you're retempering plaster, you run the risk of changing the color, as well as the strength and consistency of the plaster. Basically, each time you add more water to the plaster, you're diluting the power of the plaster mix. The key for plasterers to achieve better plaster and faster output is to make sure that they have an optimal plaster mix with longer board life.",,0,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8932,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Tools,,37.220,,Monday 13 December 2010 06:09:16 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,28.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54384,NAP-330-MX12H,ariel2,Mixtion Oil 250 ml Can (8.4 oz.) 12 Hour: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Mixtion Oil 250 ml Can (8.4 oz.) 12 Hour by Natural Pigments,0.010,23.950,23.950,,"Mixtion Oil 250 ml Can (8.4 oz.) 12 Hour <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Traditional, clear, natural oil-based size made in France. LeFranc & Bougeois has earned the reputation of being the best oil size available and experienced gilders request LeFranc for their most important projects. LeFranc size has superior levling properties and most predictable characteristics. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>LeFranc 12 Hour Size is suitable for all projects requiring a longer open time for gilding. It reaches tack in 12-14 hours, depending on film thickness, temperature and humidity, and will remain open for gilding for 8-12 hours. Le Franc 12 Hour Size requires one month to fully cure before sealing or glazing. Until fully cured, the gildered surface is fragile and should be protected from harm. The open time for gilding with metal leaf may be less, since metal leaf is heavier. Always stir LeFranc size before use. The driers in LeFranc size settle to the bottom of the container and must be stirred to produce a blended product. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Oil sizes are ready to gild when your knuckle taps the surface without disturbing the size or coming away with residue. Oil sizes may be thinned up to 10 percent with mineral spritis. If thinned, the drying time may be reduced. A soft hair brush will produce a smooth even surface. Brushes are best cleaned with mineral spritis. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Porous surfaces should be sealed to create as smooth surface for gilding. Shellac is recommended for sealing gilded surfaces on interior work.",,1000001,2,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,31.020,,Friday 12 November 2010 06:52:53 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,23.950,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54379,NAP-330-MX03H,ariel2,Mixtion Oil 250 ml Can (8.4 oz.) 3 Hour: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Mixtion Oil 250 ml Can (8.4 oz.) 3 Hour by Natural Pigments,0.010,23.950,23.950,,"Mixtion Oil 250 ml Can (8.4 oz.) 3 Hour <EOL><br><br> <EOL>Traditional, clear, natural oil-based size made in France. LeFranc & Bourgeois has earned the reputation of being the best oil size available and experienced gilders request LeFranc for their most important projects. LeFranc size has superior levling properties and most predictable characteristics. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>LeFranc 3 Hour Size reaches tack in 3-5 hours depending on film thickness, temperature and humidity. After reaching the proper gilding tack, it will remain open for gilding with genuine gold leaf for 4-6 hours. The open time for gilding with metal leaf may be less, since metal leaf is heavier. Allow the gilded surface to cure one week before sealing or glazing. Always stir LeFranc size before use. The driers in LeFranc size settle to the bottom of the container and must be stirred to produce a blended product. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Oil sizes are ready to gild when your knuckle taps the surface without disturbing the size or coming away with residue. Oil sizes may be thinned up to 10 percent with mineral spritis. If thinned, the drying time may be reduced. A soft hair brush will produce a smooth even surface. Brushes are best cleaned with mineral spritis. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Porous surfaces should be sealed to create as smooth surface for gilding. Shellac is recommended for sealing gilded surfaces on interior work. <EOL> <EOL>",,1000001,2,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,31.020,,Friday 12 November 2010 06:43:45 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,23.950,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58480,NAP-641-MRPTL5,ariel2,"Mortar and Pestle (Large), 12.7 cm (5 in.) Diameter, 600 ml (20 oz.) Capacity: Made in USA by Natural Pigments","Mortar and Pestle (Large), 12.7 cm (5 in.) Diameter, 20 oz. Capacity",0.500,12.500,12.500,,"Mortar and Pestle (Large), 12.7 cm (5 in.) Diameter, 600 ml (20 oz.) Capacity <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>White pharmaceutical porcelain mortar and pestle for grinding pigments and other materials for use in mediums and resins. The hard inner surface is unglazed allowing you to easily abrade nearly any material to the degree of fineness that you need for fine pigments. Do not use to crush stones or extremely hard materials. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Use and Care Instructions</b><br /> <EOL>Place item to be ground or crushed in the mortar. <EOL>Work the pestle with a downward pushing motion in a circular pattern. <EOL>Keep a firm grip on the pestle and be sure not to use excessive force. <EOL>Wash porcelain mortar and pestle with warm water and detergent or soap",,999996,4,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,57728,Painting and Painting Accessories/Raw Materials/Pigments,,16.720,,Monday 13 December 2010 05:00:38 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,12.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58483,NAP-641-MRPTL4,ariel2,"Mortar and Pestle (Medium), 10 cm (4.2 in.) Diameter: Made in USA by Natural Pigments","Mortar and Pestle (Medium), 10 cm (4.2 in.) Diameter ",0.500,12.500,12.500,,"Mortar and Pestle (Medium), 10 cm (4.2 in.) Diameter <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>White pharmaceutical porcelain mortar and pestle for grinding pigments and other materials for use in mediums and resins. The hard inner surface is unglazed allowing you to easily abrade nearly any material to the degree of fineness that you need for fine pigments. Do not use to crush stones or extremely hard materials. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Use and Care Instructions</b><br /> <EOL>Place item to be ground or crushed in the mortar. <EOL>Work the pestle with a downward pushing motion in a circular pattern. <EOL>Keep a firm grip on the pestle and be sure not to use excessive force. <EOL>Wash porcelain mortar and pestle with warm water and detergent or soap.",,0,1,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8932,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Tools,,15.130,,Monday 13 December 2010 05:05:07 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,12.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58487,NAP-641-MRPTL2,ariel2,"Mortar and Pestle (Small), 6 cm (2.5 in.) Diameter: Made in USA by Natural Pigments","Mortar and Pestle (Small), 6 cm (2.5 in.) Diameter",0.500,12.500,12.500,,"Mortar and Pestle (Small), 6 cm (2.5 in.) Diameter <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>White pharmaceutical porcelain mortar and pestle for grinding pigments and other materials for use in mediums and resins. The hard inner surface is unglazed allowing you to easily abrade nearly any material to the degree of fineness that you need for fine pigments. Do not use to crush stones or extremely hard materials. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Use and Care Instructions</b><br /> <EOL>Place item to be ground or crushed in the mortar. <EOL>Work the pestle with a downward pushing motion in a circular pattern. <EOL>Keep a firm grip on the pestle and be sure not to use excessive force. <EOL>Wash porcelain mortar and pestle with warm water and detergent or soap.",,999985,6,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,50263,Furniture for Artists/Lamps and Lighting,,16.720,,Monday 13 December 2010 05:08:25 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,12.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58567,NAP-682-14281,ariel2,Mortar Hoe with D Grip: 4 3/4" X 7",Mortar Hoe with D Grip: 4 3/4" X 7",0.500,24.200,24.200,,"<B>Mortar Hoe with D Grip: 4 3/4"" X 7""</b><BR><BR> <EOL><b>About Mortar Hoe with D Grip</b><BR> <EOL>The holes in the blade allow for more effective mixing of plaster and mortar in a mortar pan. The head is one piece forged from carbon steel, riveted to the steel ferrule. This hoe has a heavy-duty 45.7 cm (18-in.) hardwood handle with a sturdy ""D"" grip.",,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,31.340,,Monday 13 December 2010 07:12:53 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,24.200,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58462,NAP-631-2160,ariel2,Mouth Atomizer,Mouth Atomizer,0.200,5.750,5.750,,"<B>Mouth Atomizer</b><BR><BR> <EOL><B>About Mouth Atomizer</b><BR> <EOL>The mouth atomizer is a device that can be used to spray watercolor paint, ink or other liquids evenly over a surface. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>The mouth atomizer consists of two hinged tubes, one of which is placed into the liquid to be sprayed and the other of which is blown into by mouth. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Learning to use the atomizer is a matter of practice and of blowing hard enough to create a venturi effect between the tubes. This draws the liquid up the long tube and then propels it forward so that it sprays the desired surface. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL><B>How to Use</b><BR> <EOL>To use the mouth atomizer, first make certain that the tubes are clean and clear of obstructions or foreign matter. Examine them to ensure that you can see clearly down the tubes. If they're blocked, run a thin wire down the tube to remove the blockage. Remember, the cleaner the mouth atomizer, the better it will work. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Next, you should spread out the two legs of the atomizer to form an upside down ""L"" shape. It may be necessary to adjust the legs slightly to get the atomizer to work best, but an upside down ""L"" is very close to the perfect position. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>To use the atomizer, put the narrower tube in the liquid you want to spray and then blow onto the end of the wider tube. It's best to try this with water first. If you can spray water, you've learned how to blow correctly and can use the atomizer on other liquids. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>If you're having trouble getting anything to spray (this is common at first), it's most likely because you're not blowing hard enough. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>That’s it. It takes a bit of practice, but once you've mastered the skill you'll find that the atomizer works very well. It's probably the least expensive way to evenly spread a liquid over another surface. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL><B>Alternative Use</b><BR> <EOL>Instead of blowing with your mouth, try a can of aerosol propellant to provide the necessary force. Simply attach the wider tube from the end of the atomizer (where your mouth would blow) to the source of compressed air and let the air do all the work.",,0,3,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,6.530,,Saturday 11 December 2010 10:52:31 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,2.990,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58596,NAP-540-50108,bhavesh,Neil's Best Damar Varnish 8 fl oz (236.6 ml) Bottle: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Neil's Best Damar Varnish 8 fl oz (236.6 ml) Bottle,0.500,14.500,14.500,,"<B>Neil's Best Damar Varnish 8 fl oz (236.6 ml) Bottle, Made in USA by Natural Pigments</b><BR><BR> <EOL><b>About Neil's Best Damar Varnish</b><BR> <EOL>Neil's Best Damar Varnish is traditional varnish of damar resin dissolved without heat in pure gum turpentine and aged one year. Use Neil's Best Damar Varnish as a final glossy picture varnish over well-dried oil paintings, after 6-12 months, or add Wax Paste for satin finish. Add to oil colors for luminosity, use to make egg-oil emulsions or as quick-drying paint medium. (31% resin solution). <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL><B>Caution</b><BR> Follow safety instructions carefully. Not suitable for use by children. Shipping restrictions apply to hazardous materials. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL><B>Hazardous Material</b><BR> Cannot ship by Air or Next Day Services. Ships Ground Only. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL><b>Manufacturer’s Label Warnings</b><BR> <EOL><B>WARNING</b><BR> FLAMMABLE. MAY BE HARMFUL BY BREATHING VAPORS. EYE IRRITANT. OVEREXPOSURE MAY RESULT IN NAUSEA, HEADACHE, CONFUSION OR INSTABILITY. CONTAINS: PETROLEUM DISTILLATES. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL><B>PRECAUTIONS</b><BR> Avoid breathing vapors. Keep away from eyes. Do not store or use near heat or flame. Use exhaust fan to assure adequate cross ventilation. KEEP OUT OF REACH OF CHILDREN. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL><B>FIRST AID</b><BR> If eye irritation occurs, rinse with tap water 5-10 minutes. If irritation persists, seek medical care. If swallowed, get prompt medical attention. If symptoms occur, move to fresh air. If symptoms persist, see a physician.",,999998,2,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8967,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Varnishes,,21.170,,Monday 13 December 2010 08:01:20 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,14.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54878,NAP-510-27008,bhavesh,Neutral pH PVA Adhesive (8 oz) Bottle: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Neutral pH PVA Adhesive (8 oz) Bottle: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,0.500,8.420,8.420,,"Neutral pH PVA Adhesive (8 oz) Bottle<BR><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Neutral pH PVA Adhesive</b><BR> <EOL>Lineco Neutral pH PVA Adhesive is a white, neutral pH adhesive that dries clear and fast. It is fully reversible with water. The adhesive spreads well, and has good open time and lay flat characteristics. Dries acid-free, solvent-free and is water-soluble. <EOL><br><Br> <EOL>Lineco Neutral pH Adhesive is made of archival polyvinyl acetate (PVA). This adhesive was formulated specifically for conservation materials and will not yellow or become brittle with age. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL><b>Application</b><BR> <EOL>Lineco Neutral pH Adhesive is an excellent adhesive for bookbinding, collage or general art work. Use it to adhere paper or fabric to rigid porous supports, such as canvas on wood panel. <EOL>",,0,3,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8670,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Grounds/Neutral pH PVA Adhesives,,7.800,,Monday 15 November 2010 08:21:37 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,6.320,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54885,NAP-510-27128,bhavesh,Neutral pH PVA Adhesive Gallon (128 fl oz) Bottle: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Neutral pH PVA Adhesive Gallon (128 fl oz) Bottle by Natural Pigment,8,69,69,,"Neutral pH PVA Adhesive Gallon (128 fl oz) Bottle<BR><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Neutral pH PVA Adhesive</b><BR> <EOL>Lineco Neutral pH PVA Adhesive is a white, neutral pH adhesive that dries clear and fast. It is fully reversible with water. The adhesive spreads well, and has good open time and lay flat characteristics. Dries acid-free, solvent-free and is water-soluble. <EOL><br><Br> <EOL>Lineco Neutral pH Adhesive is made of archival polyvinyl acetate (PVA). This adhesive was formulated specifically for conservation materials and will not yellow or become brittle with age. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL><b>Application</b><BR> <EOL>Lineco Neutral pH Adhesive is an excellent adhesive for bookbinding, collage or general art work. Use it to adhere paper or fabric to rigid porous supports, such as canvas on wood panel. <EOL>",,999999,5,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8670,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Grounds/Neutral pH PVA Adhesives,,88.620,,Monday 15 November 2010 08:28:37 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,69,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54880,NAP-510-27032,bhavesh,Neutral pH PVA Adhesive Quart (32 fl oz) Bottle: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Neutral pH PVA Adhesive Quart (32 fl oz) Bottle by Natural Pigment,2,28.160,21.120,,"Neutral pH PVA Adhesive Quart (32 fl oz) Bottle<BR><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Neutral pH PVA Adhesive</b><BR> <EOL>Lineco Neutral pH PVA Adhesive is a white, neutral pH adhesive that dries clear and fast. It is fully reversible with water. The adhesive spreads well, and has good open time and lay flat characteristics. Dries acid-free, solvent-free and is water-soluble. <EOL><br><Br> <EOL>Lineco Neutral pH Adhesive is made of archival polyvinyl acetate (PVA). This adhesive was formulated specifically for conservation materials and will not yellow or become brittle with age. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL><b>Application</b><BR> <EOL>Lineco Neutral pH Adhesive is an excellent adhesive for bookbinding, collage or general art work. Use it to adhere paper or fabric to rigid porous supports, such as canvas on wood panel. <EOL>",,0,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8670,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Grounds/Neutral pH PVA Adhesives,,27.580,,Monday 15 November 2010 08:25:23 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,21.120,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54012,NAP-900-17NST,bhavesh,Nickel-Silver Thin Aluminum Point 0.9 mm (0.035 in): Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Nickel-Silver Thin Aluminum Point 0.9mm (0.035) in by Natural Pigments,0.500,5,5,,Thin Aluminum Point 0.9 mm (0.035 in) <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>Nickel-Silver Point shaped to a cone on one end. The 50 mm (2 in) length lasts through hundreds of drawings. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Fits the following metalpoint holder:</b><br /> <EOL>Metalpoint Holder 0.9 mm (0.035 in),,999999,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,57021,Brushes/Oil and Acrylic Brushes/Natural,,6.800,,Wednesday 10 November 2010 05:36:40 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,5,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54190,NAP-301-1102,bhavesh,Oil Gilding Kit Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Oil Gilding Kit Made in USA by Natural Pigments,0.250,79.400,79.400,,"The Natural Pigments Oil Gilding Kit has all the tools and supplies needed to complete an oil gilding project from start to finish. Included are the materials to apply the mordant and apply gold leaf. One book of patent gold leaf is included to start you project. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>The complete kit includes:</b><br /> <EOL>* 1 each LeFranc & Bourgeois Mixtion Size, 250 ml<br /> <EOL>* 1 each Round Squirrel Brush<br /> <EOL>* 1 each Patent Gold Leaf, 23.5 Karat, book<br /> <EOL>* Steel Wool Pads and Cotton Balls<br />",,1000001,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,76.490,,Thursday 11 November 2010 05:32:00 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,59.550,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58214,NAP-601-1102,bhavesh,Oil Paint Making Kit: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Oil Paint Making Kit: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,1,137,137,,"The Natural Pigments Oil Paint-Making Kit is intended for artists who want to expand their oil-painting horizons, but have little or no experience making their own paints. The kit comes wih all the materials that you need to get started, including instructions, basic oil medium, glass muller, grinding surface and six traditional pigments in dry powder form to start making your own oil colors. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>It is an excellent introduction to paint making, which can open the door to a new range of possibilities in oil mediums, pigments and paint recipes. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Pigments Included in the Kit</b><br /> <EOL>The kit includes one ounce volume (29 cc) each of Green Earth, Yellow Ocher, Red Ocher, Umber, Titanium White and Black—all packaged in individual plastic jars. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>Purpose of the Oil Paint-Making Kit</b><br /> <EOL>The Natural Pigments Oil Paint-Making Kit is designed for artists who wish to make small amounts of oil colors. You will find it useful for making paint on the spot, as you need them. Unlike larger grinding tools, the small size of these tools allows for easy carefree cleanup between use. It's also a great educational tool for instructors to demonstrate how artists' paint was made prior to the 19th century. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL>It is an excellent introduction to paint making, which can open the door to a new range of possibilities in different mediums, pigments and paint recipes. <EOL><br /><br /> <EOL><b>The kit includes the following items:</b><br /> <EOL>* 1 each Introductory Pigment Sampler<br /> <EOL>* 1 each Muller, glass medium, 6.3 cm (2.5 in.) diameter base<br /> <EOL>* 1 each Grinding plate, 254 x 254 x 63 mm (10 x 10 x 0.25 inch) tempered glass (This glass is not sandblasted or roughened and must be prepared before use by grinding with silicon carbide.)<br /> <EOL>* 1 each Spatula, stainless steel metal with wood handle<br /> <EOL>* 1 each Silicon carbide, 100 grit, net vol. 1 oz. (29 cc) jar<br /> <EOL>* 1 each Dispenser bottle, 8 fl oz. capacity<br /> <EOL>* 6 each Collapsible metal tubes and caps, 50 ml capacity<br /> <EOL>* 1 each Refined Linseed Oil, 8 fl oz (237 ml)<br /> <EOL>* 1 each Making Your Own Water-Solved Paint—This 12-page document contains instructions for preparing the grinding surface, making your own watercolor paint and storing paint in collapsible tubes. (This item is sent by email as a PDF document.)",,999,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,10,Y,50374,Painting and Painting Accessories/Oil Paints,,129.800,,Friday 10 December 2010 07:32:27 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,102.750,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54087,NAP-950-OMP65,ariel2,"Old Master Paper: Gaspe (Jade Green), 18"" x 24"", Made in USA by Natural Pigments","Old Master Paper: Gaspe (Jade Green), 18"" x 24"" by Natural Pigments",0.200,5.500,5.500,,"* Old Master paper made from linen and cotton rags like drawing papers of 17th and 18th centuries.<br /> <EOL>* Lightweight and strong they are excellent for calligraphy and drawing with charcoal, chalk and sanguine.<br /> <EOL>* They print well in lithography, letterpress, etching and even ink-jet.<br /> <EOL>* It has been used for historic wallpaper and book restorations.",,0,1,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8576,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Old Master Papers,,7.780,,Wednesday 10 November 2010 08:08:19 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,5.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
