56152,NAP-850-108FP,bhavesh2,Rublev Colours 3 ml Royal Smalt (Full Pan),Rublev Colours 3 ml Royal Smalt (Full Pan),0.010,10.950,10.950,,"Rublev Colours Royal Smalt (Full Pan)<BR><br> <EOL><B>Specifications</b><BR> <EOL><B>Current Names: </b><BR> <EOL>* English: smalt<BR> <EOL>* French: smalt<BR> <EOL>* German: Smalte<BR> <EOL>* Italian: azzurro di smalto, smaltino<BR> <EOL>* Japanese: hana konjō<BR> <EOL>* Russian: смальта<BR> <EOL>* Spanish: esmalte <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL><b> Synonyms:</b> <EOL>* English: starch blue<BR> <EOL>* French: azur à poudrer, bleu d'émail, émail, esmail<BR> <EOL>* German: Azurblau, Couleur, Eschel, Kaiserblau, Königsblau, Sächsischblau, Streublau<BR> <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL><B>Color Information</b><BR> <EOL>* Single Pigment: Smalt<BR> <EOL>* Binder: Gum Arabic<BR><BR> <EOL> <EOL><B> Pigment Information</b><BR> <EOL>* Color: Blue<BR> <EOL>* Colour Index: Pigment Blue 32<BR> <EOL>* Chemical Name: Potassium cobalt silicate<BR> <EOL>* Chemical Formula: KCoSi <EOL><b>Properties</b><BR> <EOL>* ASTM Lightfastness: Not Rated<BR> <EOL>* Opacity: Transparent<BR> <EOL>* Tinting Strength: High<BR> <EOL>* Staining: Low<BR> <EOL>* Granulating: High<BR><BR> <EOL><B>About Royal Smal</b><BR> <EOL>Rublev Colours Royal Smalt is an intense deep blue color used by watercolorists in the 18th and 19th centuries and used in painting since at least the 16th century, although it has been found in paintings much earlier than that time. Smalt is a moderately to coarsely ground potassium glass of blue color with a definite violet hue. The color is due to small amounts of cobalt added during the manufacturing process. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL><B>Note:</b> Colors swatches are shown in mass tone, at top, mixed with an equal amount of water and brushed out toward the bottom. All pictures of color swatches in this web site are only approximations of the actual color of the watercolor paint. We have taken every care to match the color in these pictures on calibrated color monitors to the actual color. However, because of the wide variance in color monitors the results you get may vary<BR><BR> <EOL><B><Font Color=Red>Due to the large particles of this color, we recommend using this watercolor only with rough watercolor paper or with additional watercolor medium to aid the large particles to adhere to the paper.</b></font>",,1000000,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,7.550,,Monday 22 November 2010 11:03:38 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,5.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
