58063,NAP-261-312,bhavesh,Rublev Colours Italian Raw Sienna 2 fl oz (59 ml) Bottle,Rublev Colours Italian Raw Sienna 2 fl oz (59 ml) Bottle,0.130,11.950,11.950,,"Rublev Colours Italian Raw Sienna 2 fl oz (59 ml) Bottle<br><Br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><BR> <EOL><B>Common Names</B><BR> <EOL>* English: sienna<BR> <EOL>* French: terre de sienne<BR> <EOL>* German: Sienaerde<BR> <EOL>* Italian: terra di siena<BR> <EOL>* Russian: сиена<BR> <EOL>* Spanish: tierra de siena<BR><BR> <EOL><B>Nomenclature</B><BR> <EOL>* Common name: Sienna<BR> <EOL>* Primary Mineral: Goethite <BR> <EOL>* Source: Tuscany, Italy<BR><BR> <EOL><B>Pigment Information</b><BR> <EOL>* Color: Brown<BR> <EOL>* Colour Index: Pigment Brown 6 (77491)<BR> <EOL>* Chemical Name: Iron Oxide Hydroxide <BR> <EOL>* Chemical Formula: α-FeOOH<BR><BR> <EOL><B>ASTM Lightfastness Rating</b><BR> <EOL>* Acrylic: 	I<BR> <EOL>* Watercolor: I<BR> <EOL>* Oil: I<BR><BR> <EOL><B>Properties</b><BR> <EOL>* Density: 3.3–4.3<BR> <EOL>* Hardness: 5.0–5.5<BR> <EOL>* Refractive Index: nα=2.260 nβ=2.393 nγ=2.398<BR><BR> <EOL><B>About Sienna</b><BR> <EOL>Sienna is an iron oxide earth pigment that resembles yellow ocher. Unlike yellow ocher, which generally are opaque, sienna earths are more translucent and warmer. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Rublev Colours Aqueous Dispersions are pigments dispersed in water ready to be mixed with water-based mediums. These dispersions are especially made for use with traditional painting mediums, such as egg tempera, casein tempera, fresco, watercolors and distemper (glue tempera). They are also ideally suited for use with gesso to make toned grounds for drawing and painting. Pigment dispersions from Rublev Colours contain only naturally-derived ingredients, in addition to pigment and water, making them ideally suited for traditional mediums. Unlike other pigment dispersions that are typically made for acrylic medium, Rublev Colours Aqueous Dispersions do not contain coalescent solvents, artificial dispersing 