the content of iron oxide and other minerals, the color of red ochre varies from deep red to brownish red. Red iron oxide minerals, such as hematite, are found around the world and have been used as pigments since prehistory.<BR><BR> <EOL><B>Permanence and Compatibility</b><BR> <EOL>Red ochres are among the most permanent colors among the artist's palette. It is compatible with all other pigments, and can be used with good results in all mediums.<BR><BR> <EOL><B>Oil Absorption and Grinding</b><BR> <EOL>Red ochres absorb a medium amount of oil, which may slow the drying of oil paint, but because iron oxide is a drier in oil, it dries fast and forms an excellent film.<BR><BR> <EOL><B>Toxicity</b><BR> <EOL>Red ochres are not considered toxic, but care should be used in handling the dry powder pigment to avoid inhaling the dust.",,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,135.460,,Wednesday 01 December 2010 06:00:59 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,114,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
