minated rags will remove contaminating materials and eliminate risk.",,1000000,1,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,19.520,,Tuesday 16 November 2010 09:17:53 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,8.580,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55149,NAP-510-40OST08,bhavesh,Sun-Thickened Linseed Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Sun-Thickened Linseed Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle by Natural Pigments,0.500,34,34,,"Sun-Thickened Linseed Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle<BR><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><BR> <EOL>* Natural Source: Linseed Linum usitatissimum<bR> <EOL>* Acid Value (mg KOH/g), max: 4 <br> <EOL>* Color (Gardner 1953), max.: 3 <br> <EOL>* Iodine Value: 	145-160 <br> <EOL>* Viscosity (Stokes @ 25° C): 4.35<br> <EOL>* Viscosity (Gardner-Holdt @ 25° C): Q<br> <EOL>* Saponification Value: 162-172<br> <EOL>* Appearance: Clear/Transparent at 25° C<br> <EOL>* Specific gravity: 0.960 @ 25° C<br> <EOL>* Weight Per Gallon: 7.81 lbs.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Epoxide Oil</b><BR> <EOL>Natural Pigments Sun-Bleached Linseed Oil is made by exposing raw, cold-pressed linseed oil to sunlight in shallow enamel trays covered with clear glass but exposed to the atomosphere for a period of less than one month. No driers or other additives are used in the making of this oil. The exposure to sunlight lightens the considerably and only slightly thickens it. This linseed oil has about the same color as walnut oil, so it can be used with pale colors and white. This oil can be used as a medium or added to homemade mediums. <EOL><BR><br> <EOL>Use turpentine or mineral spirits as a solvent or diluent for oil painting mediums made with linseed oil. Linseed oil is a yellowish drying oil derived from the dried ripe seeds of the flax plant (Linum usitatissimum, Linaceae). <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL><B>Warning:</b><br> Rags or paper towels contaminated with vegetable drying oils, particularly those containing iron oxide pigments are susceptible to spontaneous combustion. To prevent unexpected fires, used rags or paper towels contaminated with oil-based materials should be collected in a closeable, air-tight container. Store water-dampened rags or paper towels in a metal container with an air-tight top. Alternately, washing contaminated rags will remove contaminating materials and eliminate risk.",,1000000,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,30.540,,Tuesday 16 November 2010 09:13:40 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,25.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58491,NAP-650-SFKNTWB,bhavesh2,Surface Knife (Twin Blade): 4 3/4" Wide x 4 1/8" Tall,Surface Knife (Twin Blade): 4 3/4" Wide x 4 1/8" Tall ,0.500,24.500,24.500,,"<B>Surface Knife (Twin Blade): 4 3/4"" Wide x 4 1/8"" Tall </b><BR><BR> <EOL><b>About Surface Knife</b><BR> <EOL>We selected this German-made surface knife as the cadillac of scrapers, because of its twin blade and comfortable wood grip. It makes scraping or applying a gesso surface onto a panel easier. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>This polished steel knife has a hand-shaped, varnished wood grip. The blade has a finger rest-plate for even distribution of pressure across the entire width of the blade. Slight rounding of the blade ends ensures a smooth application of materials, such as gesso, in only one operation. The flexibility of the knife blade can be accurately set by adjusting the finger rest-plate. The first-class, electrically-hardnened stainless steel blade is machine ground for maximum durability and a lifetime of wear. The precision-hardened blade measures 120 mm (4-3/4 in.) wide by 105 mm (4-1/8 in.) tall.",,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8932,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Tools,,31.730,,Monday 13 December 2010 05:11:29 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,24.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58499,NAP-651-SFKN105,bhavesh2,Surface Knife: 105 mm Wide,Surface Knife: 105 mm Wide,0.500,10,10,,"<B>Surface Knife: 105 mm Wide</b><BR><BR> <EOL><b>About Surface Knife</b><BR> <EOL>We chose this German-made scraper because it is ideal for scraping a gesso surface. This smoothing scraper, also called a ""Japan"" scraper, has an aluminum handle without rivets, so it is easy to grip and permits easy cleaning by simply throwing it into water or thinner. The first-class, electrically-hardnened stainless steel blade is machine ground for maximum durability and a lifetime of wear. The precision-hardened blade measures 105 mm (4-1/8 in.) wide by 105 mm (4-1/8 in.) tall.",,999998,2,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8932,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Tools,,13.480,,Monday 13 December 2010 05:18:37 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,10,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58496,NAP-651-SFKN080,bhavesh2,Surface Knife: 80 mm Wide,Surface Knife: 80 mm Wide,0.500,8,8,,"<B>Surface Knife: 80 mm Wide</b><BR><BR> <EOL><b>About Surface Knife</b><BR> <EOL>We chose this German-made scraper because it is ideal for scraping a gesso surface. This smoothing scraper, also called a ""Japan"" scraper, has an aluminum handle without rivets, so it is easy to grip and permits easy cleaning by simply throwing it into water or thinner. The first-class, electrically-hardnened stainless steel blade is machine ground for maximum durability and a lifetime of wear. The precision-hardened blade measures 80 mm (3-1/4 in.) wide by 105 mm (4-1/8 in.) tall.",,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8932,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Tools,,10.790,,Monday 13 December 2010 05:15:50 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,8,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54579,NAP-510-13TAL1K,bhavesh,Talc 1 kg (2.2 lbs) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Talc 1 kg (2.2 lbs) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,2.200,6.850,6.850,,"Talc 1 kg (2.2 lbs) Bag<BR><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><BR> <EOL>* Description: A fine dry ground talc with a closely-controlled particle size distribution.<br> <EOL>* Source: Montana<br><br> <EOL><b>Chemical Analysis</b><br> <EOL>* Calcium carbonate: 98%</b><BR> <EOL>* Magnesium carbonate: <1%<br><br> <EOL><b> Typical Physical Properties</b><BR> <EOL>* Y Brightness: 92<br> <EOL>* Retained on 325 Mesh Screen: 1%<br> <EOL>* Moisture Loss @110° C.: 0.03%<bR> <EOL>* Oil Absorption: 8.5 g oil / 100 g pigment<br> <EOL>* Apparent Bulk Density, Packed:	0.80 g/cc (50.0 lbs./ft3)<br> <EOL>* Apparent Bulk Density, Loose: 1.50 g/cc (93.5 lbs./ft3)<br> <EOL>* Specific Gravity: 2.7<br> <EOL>* Median Particle Size: 12 microns<bR><BR> <EOL><b>About Talc</b><BR> <EOL>Brilliant white, fine talc for making grounds, paint and pastels. Our talc is dry ground from natural ores in Montana. Use as an additive to make grounds and for adding texture and body to paints. <EOL><br> <EOL>Add to oil colors and mediums to create textural and bodying qualities to oil paint without affecting the color. Chalk has little color in drying oil, so it can be added to oil paint without affecting the tint of the color.",,999988,3,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,50263,Furniture for Artists/Lamps and Lighting,,6.990,,Saturday 13 November 2010 06:18:58 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,5.140,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54860,NAP-510-21THGLK,bhavesh,Technical Gelatin 1 Kg (2.2 lbs) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Technical Gelatin 1 Kg (2.2 lbs) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,2.200,22,22,,"Technical Gelatin 1 Kg (2.2 lbs) Bag<BR><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Technical Gelatin</b><BR> <EOL>This is a technical grade of gelatin made in the U.S. It is a fine mesh granular gelatin that is easy to dissolve in water. The technical grade means that it is the lightest in color and most translucsent grade available. This makes it ideal for use in gilding. Gelatin is preferred by many professional gilders over hide glue, because it can take a super burnish easier than hide glue when mixed with gilder's clay or gesso. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Gelatin glue is graded and sold by its Bloom Value. Bloom value is a measurement of the strength of a gel formed by a 6 and 2/3% solution of the glue that has been kept in a constant temperature bath at 10° C for 18 hours. A device called a Texture Analyzer is then used to measure the weight in grams required to depress a standard plunger 4 millimeters into the gel. If this procedure requires 200 grams, then the glue is a 200-bloom value glue. Glue is also tested for its viscosity at this same 6 and 2/3% concentration. A standard viscosity range is associated with each bloom level. <EOL><Br><Br> <EOL><b>Preparation Directions</b><BR> <EOL>First soak in water for 30 minutes and then gently heat in a water bath until completely dissolved. Apply with a brush while warm or with a spatula when allowed to cool to room temperature (it will gel when cool). For gilding, use as an adhesive for metal leaf, such as gold leaf. Mix with gilder's clay or whiting to make a base for gilding. Add calcium carbonate (calcite, chalk or marble dust) for chalk grounds or calcium sulfate (gypsum) for gesso grounds. Always make the minimum concentration required; as a guide, a set gel should be somewhere between hard set and liquid -- about the consistency of jelly. For gilding size, use 40 grams for every liter (quart) of water. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><Br> <EOL>* Bloom: 200 grams<br> <EOL>The bloom value refers to the strength of a gel formed by a 6 and 2/3% solution of the glue kept at a constant temperature. The higher the number the greater the strength of the glue.<br><BR> <EOL>* Viscosity: 140 - 160 millipascal seconds<br> <EOL>Millipascal seconds is the measurement of viscosity which is measured by the flow velocity of the glue solution through a funnel.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Distemper Paint Recipe</b><Br> <EOL>Hide glue and gelatin both provide a low cost, easily formulated paint that is called distemper. Diluted with water, it is good for color sketching, as well as for painting. Distemper paintings have lasted for centuries without change.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>Ingredients</b><BR> <EOL>* 1 part Technical Gelatin(dry)<br> <EOL>* 10 parts water<br><bR> <EOL> <EOL>Soak the glue in water for 30 minutes to one hour.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL>Warm this swollen glue by placing the container in another vessel filled with hot tap water. This will cause the glue to completely dissolve. Never heat collagen glue over 60° C (140° F).<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>How to Use</b><BR> <EOL>Work dry pigments with water into a heavy paste using a palette knife. Then grind the pigment paste into the warm solution of glue. Keep the paints warm enough to remain in solution while painting with them, and use warm water to dilute them. Use a bristle brush for painting, applying the paint in thin layers to glue-sized paper, cardboard, wood panel or canvas. This method is excellent for alla prima painting and for thin underpainting. To harden and preserve the paint film, spray the dried painting with a 10% solution of water and alum. <EOL>",,999996,2,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8678,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Grounds/Perlite & Technical Gelatin Bags,,28.730,,Monday 15 November 2010 08:04:03 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,22,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54869,NAP-510-21THGLU,bhavesh,Technical Gelatin 500 g (1.1 lbs) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Technical Gelatin 500 g (1.1 lbs) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,1.100,12.950,12.950,,"Technical Gelatin 500 g (1.1 lbs) Bag<BR><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Technical Gelatin</b><BR> <EOL>This is a technical grade of gelatin made in the U.S. It is a fine mesh granular gelatin that is easy to dissolve in water. The technical grade means that it is the lightest in color and most translucsent grade available. This makes it ideal for use in gilding. Gelatin is preferred by many professional gilders over hide glue, because it can take a super burnish easier than hide glue when mixed with gilder's clay or gesso. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Gelatin glue is graded and sold by its Bloom Value. Bloom value is a measurement of the strength of a gel formed by a 6 and 2/3% solution of the glue that has been kept in a constant temperature bath at 10° C for 18 hours. A device called a Texture Analyzer is then used to measure the weight in grams required to depress a standard plunger 4 millimeters into the gel. If this procedure requires 200 grams, then the glue is a 200-bloom value glue. Glue is also tested for its viscosity at this same 6 and 2/3% concentration. A standard viscosity range is associated with each bloom level. <EOL><Br><Br> <EOL><b>Preparation Directions</b><BR> <EOL>First soak in water for 30 minutes and then gently heat in a water bath until completely dissolved. Apply with a brush while warm or with a spatula when allowed to cool to room temperature (it will gel when cool). For gilding, use as an adhesive for metal leaf, such as gold leaf. Mix with gilder's clay or whiting to make a base for gilding. Add calcium carbonate (calcite, chalk or marble dust) for chalk grounds or calcium sulfate (gypsum) for gesso grounds. Always make the minimum concentration required; as a guide, a set gel should be somewhere between hard set and liquid -- about the consistency of jelly. For gilding size, use 40 grams for every liter (quart) of water. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><Br> <EOL>* Bloom: 200 grams<br> <EOL>The bloom value refers to the strength of a gel formed by a 6 and 2/3% solution of the glue kept at a constant temperature. The higher the number the greater the strength of the glue.<br><BR> <EOL>* Viscosity: 140 - 160 millipascal seconds<br> <EOL>Millipascal seconds is the measurement of viscosity which is measured by the flow velocity of the glue solution through a funnel.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Distemper Paint Recipe</b><Br> <EOL>Hide glue and gelatin both provide a low cost, easily formulated paint that is called distemper. Diluted with water, it is good for color sketching, as well as for painting. Distemper paintings have lasted for centuries without change.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>Ingredients</b><BR> <EOL>* 1 part Technical Gelatin(dry)<br> <EOL>* 10 parts water<br><bR> <EOL> <EOL>Soak the glue in water for 30 minutes to one hour.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL>Warm this swollen glue by placing the container in another vessel filled with hot tap water. This will cause the glue to completely dissolve. Never heat collagen glue over 60° C (140° F).<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>How to Use</b><BR> <EOL>Work dry pigments with water into a heavy paste using a palette knife. Then grind the pigment paste into the warm solution of glue. Keep the paints warm enough to remain in solution while painting with them, and use warm water to dilute them. Use a bristle brush for painting, applying the paint in thin layers to glue-sized paper, cardboard, wood panel or canvas. This method is excellent for alla prima painting and for thin underpainting. To harden and preserve the paint film, spray the dried painting with a 10% solution of water and alum. <EOL>",,999998,1,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8678,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Grounds/Perlite & Technical Gelatin Bags,,17.320,,Monday 15 November 2010 08:11:46 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,12.950,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54727,NAP-510-11TRA1K,bhavesh,Terra Alba 1 kg (2.20 lbs) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Terra Alba 1 kg (2.20 lbs) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,2.200,7.500,7.500,,Terra Alba 1 kg (2.20 lbs) Bag<BR><br> <EOL><b>About Terra Alba</b><BR> <EOL>Use natural gypsum as an extender in paint and filler in gesso. Brightness is 89 median particle size is 12 microns and this product is 98% pure calcium sulfate. Oil atsorption is 23 grams of oil per 100 grams of terra alba.,,999997,2,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8681,"Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Grounds/Terra Alba, Vicenza Earth & White Kaolinite with Bags",,10.190,,Saturday 13 November 2010 10:34:13 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,7.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
