53967,NAP-900-12SHT,bhavesh2,Thin Sterling Silverpoint 0.9 mm (0.035 in): Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Thin Sterling Silverpoint 0.9 mm (0.035 in) by Natural Pigments,0.500,10,10,," <EOL>* Sterling Silverpoint made from half-hard, sterling silver and shaped to a cone on one end.<br /> <EOL>* The 50 mm (2 in) length lasts through hundreds of drawings.<br /> <EOL>* Fits the following metalpoint holder:<br /> <EOL>* Metalpoint Holder 0.9 mm (0.035 in)",,999997,4,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8551,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Points 0.9 mm,,14.430,,Tuesday 09 November 2010 11:09:41 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,10,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54001,NAP-900-14BDT,bhavesh2,Thin Yellow Brass Point 0.9 mm (0.035 in): Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Thin Yellow Brass Point 0.9 mm (0.035 in) by Natural Pigments,0.500,5,5,, <EOL>* Brass Point shaped to a cone on one end.<br /> <EOL>* The 50 mm (2 in) length lasts through hundreds of drawings.<br /> <EOL>* Fits the following metalpoint holder:<br /> <EOL>* Metalpoint Holder 0.9 mm (0.035 in),,999993,6,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8551,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Points 0.9 mm,,6.800,,Wednesday 10 November 2010 05:00:58 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,5,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53843,NAP-635-GES158,rommel,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Basic Shape Set, Made in USA by Natural Pigments",Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Basic Shape Set by Natural Pigments,2,139,139,,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Basic Shape Set<bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>Dimensions</b><BR> <EOL>* Cone measures 8-1/2 inches high and a base diameter of 5-1/2 inches;<br> <EOL>* Sphere 5-1/2 inches in diameter;<br> <EOL>* Cylinder is 8 inches high and is 4-1/4 inches in diameter;<br> <EOL>* Cube is 5-1/2 inches in all dimensions;<br> <EOL>* Dodecahedron (twelve-sided shape) is 6-1/2 inches in all dimensions.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL>This set of Basic Geometric Shapes is great for studying the tonal values (highlights, shadows and half tints) of simple shapes in drawing and painting. This set is ideal for teaching perspective, beginning still life, and tonal drawing and painting. They are ideal for classroom or studio use. Included in this five piece set is a cone, sphere, cylinder, cube and dodecahedron (a regular polyhedron with twelve flat faces, also called a Platonic solid), accurately cast in brilliant white plaster. Each basic shape measures almost six inches wide with the cone and cylinder standing about 8 inches tall. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Traditionally, cast drawing has provided an excellent way for the study of proportions, shape relationships and the effect of light and shadows. Once the plaster casts are set up, they remain in place and can be drawn session after session in the same position and lighting condition. Plaster casts are ideal for drawing using the “sight-size” method or the triangulation method, another form of measuring, to reproduce shapes and relationships accurately. <EOL>",,1000000,5,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8552,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Plaster Casts,,139,,Monday 08 November 2010 11:17:31 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,104.250,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53850,NAP-635-GES1591,bhavesh2,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Ear, Made in USA by Natural Pigments",Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Ear by Natural Pigments,2,40,40,,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Ear<bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL>This larger-than-life ear plaster cast is perfect for studying proportions of the human ear. The cast has a flat back, is hollowed out to reduce weight and also features a metal wire loop for hanging. The ear cast measures 9 inches high by 6 inches wide by 3 inches deep. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Traditionally, cast drawing has provided an excellent way for the study of proportions, shape relationships and the effect of light and shadows on the human figure. Once the plaster casts are set up, they remain in place and can be drawn session after session in the same position and lighting condition. Plaster casts are ideal for drawing using the “sight-size” method or the triangulation method, another form of measuring, to reproduce shapes and relationships accurately. <EOL>",,1000000,2,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8552,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Plaster Casts,,38.830,,Monday 08 November 2010 11:27:32 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,30,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53889,NAP-635-GES1593,bhavesh,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Eye, Made in USA by Natural Pigments","Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Eye, Made in USA by Natural Pigments",2,40,40,,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Eye<bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL> <EOL>This larger-than-life mouth plaster cast is perfect for studying proportions of the human ear. The cast has a flat back, is hollowed out to reduce weight and also features a metal wire loop for hanging. The mouth cast measures 6 inches high by 7 inches wide by 3 inches deep <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Traditionally, cast drawing has provided an excellent way for the study of proportions, shape relationships and the effect of light and shadows on the human figure. Once the plaster casts are set up, they remain in place and can be drawn session after session in the same position and lighting condition. Plaster casts are ideal for drawing using the “sight-size” method or the triangulation method, another form of measuring, to reproduce shapes and relationships accurately.",,1000000,2,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8552,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Plaster Casts,,40,,Tuesday 09 November 2010 08:35:48 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,30,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53835,NAP-635-GES138,rommel,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Face (Planar), Made in USA by Natural Pigments",Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Face (Planar)  by Natural Pigments,2,65,65,,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Face (Planar)<bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL>Plaster Cast of a Face (planar) is a copy of one of the famous sculptures of Beethoven's face, divided into planar shapes. This life-sized cast is excellent for studying portraiture and the structure of the face. It can also be used in still lifes. An integral wire loop makes it easy to hang on a wall. <EOL> <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Traditionally, cast drawing has provided an excellent way for the study of proportions, shape relationships and the effect of light and shadows on the human figure. Once the plaster casts are set up, they remain in place and can be drawn session after session in the same position and lighting condition. Plaster casts are ideal for drawing using the “sight-size” method or the triangulation method, another form of measuring, to reproduce shapes and relationships accurately. <EOL> <EOL>",,1000000,1,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8552,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Plaster Casts,,66.630,,Monday 08 November 2010 10:55:12 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,48.750,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53846,NAP-635-GES159,bhavesh2,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Face Set, Made in USA by Natural Pigments out of stock",Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Face Set by Natural Pigments,2,150,150,,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Face Set<bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL>These larger-than-life face plaster casts are perfect for studying the features of the human face. Each cast has a flat back, is hollowed out to reduce weight and also features a metal wire loop for hanging. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Traditionally, cast drawing has provided an excellent way for the study of proportions, shape relationships and the effect of light and shadows on the human figure. Once the plaster casts are set up, they remain in place and can be drawn session after session in the same position and lighting condition. Plaster casts are ideal for drawing using the “sight-size” method or the triangulation method, another form of measuring, to reproduce shapes and relationships accurately. <EOL>",,1000000,1,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8552,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Plaster Casts,,144.150,,Monday 08 November 2010 11:21:20 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,112.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53837,NAP-635-GES139,rommel,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Face, Made in USA by Natural Pigments","Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Face, Made in USA by Natural Pigments",2,60,60,,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Face<bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL>Plaster Cast of a Face (planar) is a copy of one of the famous sculptures of Beethoven's face, divided into planar shapes. This life-sized cast is excellent for studying portraiture and the structure of the face. It can also be used in still lifes. An integral wire loop makes it easy to hang on a wall. <EOL> <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Traditionally, cast drawing has provided an excellent way for the study of proportions, shape relationships and the effect of light and shadows on the human figure. Once the plaster casts are set up, they remain in place and can be drawn session after session in the same position and lighting condition. Plaster casts are ideal for drawing using the “sight-size” method or the triangulation method, another form of measuring, to reproduce shapes and relationships accurately. <EOL> <EOL>",,1000000,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8552,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Plaster Casts,,57.980,,Monday 08 November 2010 10:59:11 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,45,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53834,NAP-635-GES102,rommel,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Female Torso, Made in USA by Natural Pigments",Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Female Torso by Natural Pigments,2,110,110,,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Female Torso<bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL>This female torso is 20 inches high and has a base that measures 9-1/2 by 6 inches. It stands upright on its base and is sculpted three dimensionally. Light this plaster cast with a variety of lighting to draw studies of the abdomen, back, and sides of the female figure. This is an excellent cast for classroom use, for your own figure drawings in the studio, and for use in still life compositions. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Traditionally, cast drawing has provided an excellent way for the study of proportions, shape relationships and the effect of light and shadows on the human figure. Once the plaster casts are set up, they remain in place and can be drawn session after session in the same position and lighting condition. Plaster casts are ideal for drawing using the “sight-size” method or the triangulation method, another form of measuring, to reproduce shapes and relationships accurately. <EOL>",,1000000,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8552,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Plaster Casts,,105.850,,Monday 08 November 2010 10:49:10 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,82.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53895,NAP-635-GES162,rommel,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Foot, Made in USA by Natural Pigments","Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Foot, Made in USA by Natural Pigments",2,35,35,,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Foot<bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL>This foot plaster cast is perfect for studying the proportions of the male foot in a stepping position. The foot (over 10 inches high) is cast on a base that measures 11 inches long by five inches wide by one inch high. The foot is slightly larger-than-life to make it accessible for drawing at a distance. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Traditionally, cast drawing has provided an excellent way for the study of proportions, shape relationships and the effect of light and shadows on the human figure. Once the plaster casts are set up, they remain in place and can be drawn session after session in the same position and lighting condition. Plaster casts are ideal for drawing using the “sight-size” method or the triangulation method, another form of measuring, to reproduce shapes and relationships accurately.",,1000000,1,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8552,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Plaster Casts,,35,,Tuesday 09 November 2010 08:43:27 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,26.250,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53893,NAP-635-GES160,rommel,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Hand, Made in USA by Natural Pigments","Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Hand, Made in USA by Natural Pigments",2,35,35,,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Hand<bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL> <EOL>This closed hand plaster cast is perfect for studying the proportions of the male hand in a grip position. The hand is cast on a base that measures five inches square by one inch high. The hand is slightly larger-than-life to make it accessible for drawing at a distance. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Traditionally, cast drawing has provided an excellent way for the study of proportions, shape relationships and the effect of light and shadows on the human figure. Once the plaster casts are set up, they remain in place and can be drawn session after session in the same position and lighting condition. Plaster casts are ideal for drawing using the “sight-size” method or the triangulation method, another form of measuring, to reproduce shapes and relationships accurately.",,1000000,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8552,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Plaster Casts,,34.040,,Tuesday 09 November 2010 08:40:48 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,26.250,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53838,NAP-635-GES141,rommel,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Head (Anatomical), Made in USA by Natural Pigments",Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Head (Anatomical) by Natural Pigments,2,99,99,,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Head (Anatomical)<bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL>This Life-Sized, Anatomical Human Head on a base is great for learning facial anatomy, understanding facial muscles and proportions, and for learning portraiture and drawing techniques. It is also makes a wonderful piece for still life compositions. The face is shown with one eye closed and one eye opened; and has the cheek and neck musculature exposed. Any way that you light this head, you will be inspired to draw, paint, photograph or simply enjoy it as a work of art. The plaster cast is well crafted with details of muscles and tissue. Overall, the head, neck and base measure 22 inches tall. The face is approximately 10 inches high, and the cubical base is approximately 6-1/2 inches wide, high and deep. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Traditionally, cast drawing has provided an excellent way for the study of proportions, shape relationships and the effect of light and shadows on the human figure. Once the plaster casts are set up, they remain in place and can be drawn session after session in the same position and lighting condition. Plaster casts are ideal for drawing using the “sight-size” method or the triangulation method, another form of measuring, to reproduce shapes and relationships accurately. <EOL>",,1000000,1,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8552,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Plaster Casts,,99,,Monday 08 November 2010 11:01:42 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,74.250,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53841,NAP-635-GES148,bhavesh2,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Male Arm (Anatomical), Made in USA by Natural Pigments",Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Male Arm (Anatomical),2,99,99,,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Male Arm (Anatomical)<bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL> <EOL>This Life-Sized Male Arm shows the musculature of the shoulder, arm and hand. The hand is clenched in a fist and the muscles are flexed. This cast makes a great sculpture for drawing, whether you use the entire arm or only the hand. The length is approximately 18 inches (shoulder to elbow), and the highest and widest part of the shoulder is 10 by 7 inches. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Traditionally, cast drawing has provided an excellent way for the study of proportions, shape relationships and the effect of light and shadows on the human figure. Once the plaster casts are set up, they remain in place and can be drawn session after session in the same position and lighting condition. Plaster casts are ideal for drawing using the “sight-size” method or the triangulation method, another form of measuring, to reproduce shapes and relationships accurately.",,1000000,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8552,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Plaster Casts,,95.320,,Monday 08 November 2010 11:13:03 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,74.250,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53840,NAP-635-GES147,bhavesh2,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Male Face (Planar), Made in USA by Natural Pigments",Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Male Face (Planar) by Natural Pigment,2,65,65,,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Male Face (Planar)<bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL>This Life-Sized Male Face is a study of the planes making up the human face. The face is divided into its basic shapes, facilitating teaching and self-instruction of the shape of the face. It is an ideal cast for learning facial structure, for portrait classes, or simply as a three dimensional reference. The wire hook on the back allows it to be easily hung on a wall while drawing. It can also be placed flat on a table. The face is 15 inches tall by 10 inches wide and has a depth of 7 inches. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Traditionally, cast drawing has provided an excellent way for the study of proportions, shape relationships and the effect of light and shadows on the human figure. Once the plaster casts are set up, they remain in place and can be drawn session after session in the same position and lighting condition. Plaster casts are ideal for drawing using the “sight-size” method or the triangulation method, another form of measuring, to reproduce shapes and relationships accurately.",,1000000,3,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8552,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Plaster Casts,,66.630,,Monday 08 November 2010 11:08:16 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,48.750,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53839,NAP-635-GES142,rommel,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Male Torso (Anatomical), Made in USA by Natural Pigments",Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Male Torso (Anatomical),2,35,35,,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Male Torso (Anatomical)<bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL>This Anatomical Male Torso measures 12 inches tall with a base that measures 4-1/2 by 3 inches. It stands upright and is sculpted in all three dimensions. Light this detailed plaster cast in any way to draw studies of the abdomen, back and sides of the male figure. This is a great cast for classroom use, to make figure studies in your studio, and for use in still life compositions. Although small, this cast features the main muscle groups of the male torso. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Traditionally, cast drawing has provided an excellent way for the study of proportions, shape relationships and the effect of light and shadows on the human figure. Once the plaster casts are set up, they remain in place and can be drawn session after session in the same position and lighting condition. Plaster casts are ideal for drawing using the “sight-size” method or the triangulation method, another form of measuring, to reproduce shapes and relationships accurately. <EOL> <EOL>",,1000000,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8552,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Plaster Casts,,34.040,,Monday 08 November 2010 11:04:47 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,26.250,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53887,NAP-635-GES1592,bhavesh2,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Mouth, Made in USA by Natural Pigments",Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Mouth by Natural Pigments,2,40,40,,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Mouth<bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL> <EOL>This larger-than-life mouth plaster cast is perfect for studying proportions of the human ear. The cast has a flat back, is hollowed out to reduce weight and also features a metal wire loop for hanging. The mouth cast measures 6 inches high by 7 inches wide by 3 inches deep <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Traditionally, cast drawing has provided an excellent way for the study of proportions, shape relationships and the effect of light and shadows on the human figure. Once the plaster casts are set up, they remain in place and can be drawn session after session in the same position and lighting condition. Plaster casts are ideal for drawing using the “sight-size” method or the triangulation method, another form of measuring, to reproduce shapes and relationships accurately.",,1000000,1,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8552,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Plaster Casts,,38.830,,Tuesday 09 November 2010 08:31:58 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,30,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53891,NAP-635-GES1594,bhavesh2,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Nose, Made in USA by Natural Pigments",Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Nose by Natural Pigments,2,40,40,,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Nose<bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL> <EOL>This larger-than-life mouth plaster cast is perfect for studying proportions of the human ear. The cast has a flat back, is hollowed out to reduce weight and also features a metal wire loop for hanging. The mouth cast measures 6 inches high by 7 inches wide by 3 inches deep <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Traditionally, cast drawing has provided an excellent way for the study of proportions, shape relationships and the effect of light and shadows on the human figure. Once the plaster casts are set up, they remain in place and can be drawn session after session in the same position and lighting condition. Plaster casts are ideal for drawing using the “sight-size” method or the triangulation method, another form of measuring, to reproduce shapes and relationships accurately.",,1000000,2,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8552,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Plaster Casts,,40,,Tuesday 09 November 2010 08:38:27 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,30,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53898,NAP-635-GES167,rommel,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Skull Set (Male/Female), Made in USA by Natural Pigments",Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Skull Set (Male/Female),2,90,90,,"Torino Classic Studio Sculpture: Skull Set (Male/Female)<bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL>This set of life-size Caucasian male and female skulls cast in plaster are ideal for drawing and sculpting anatomical reference, in addition to facial reconstruction study. They also make wonderful props for still life compositions or when acting in Shakespeare’s Hamlet. Light these skulls in any way to be inspired to draw, paint, photograph, or just enjoy as a work of art. The detailed casting show all major bones of the human head, making a low cost alternative to purchasing resin cast or genuine human skulls. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL> <EOL>Traditionally, cast drawing has provided an excellent way for the study of proportions, shape relationships and the effect of light and shadows on the human figure. Once the plaster casts are set up, they remain in place and can be drawn session after session in the same position and lighting condition. Plaster casts are ideal for drawing using the “sight-size” method or the triangulation method, another form of measuring, to reproduce shapes and relationships accurately. <EOL>",,1000000,1,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8552,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Drawing Plaster Casts,,90,,Tuesday 09 November 2010 08:47:06 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,67.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55025,NAP-510-14520,bhavesh,Traditional Fresco Plaster 3.5 Gal (55 lb) 25 kg Pail: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Traditional Fresco Plaster 3.5 Gal (55 lb) 25 kg P by Natural Pigments,55,90,90,,Traditional Fresco Plaster 3.5 Gal (55 lb) 25 kg Pail<BR><br> <EOL><b>About Traditional Fresco Plaster</b><br> <EOL>Traditional Fresco Plaster is a ready-to-use blend of aged lime putty and well-graded fine sharp sand in a reclosable 3.5 gal. (13.25 L) pail. Use for finish or intonaco coat of fresco paintings. Coverage is about 18 sq. ft. (1.67 m2) when applied 1/4 inch (6 mm) thick. Cured color is white. One year shelf life. All natural and aged at least 30 days. <EOL>,,999999,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8731,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Vehicles & Mediums/Fresco Plasters,,80.340,,Tuesday 16 November 2010 05:48:08 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,67.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55033,NAP-510-14720,bhavesh,Traditional Fresco Plaster with Pozzolana 3.5 Gal (58 lb) 26 kg Pail: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Traditional Fresco Plaster with Pozzolana 3.5 Gal (58 lb) 26 kg Pail,58,96,96,,"Traditional Fresco Plaster with Pozzolana 3.5 Gal (58 lb) 26 kg Pail<BR><br> <EOL><b>About Traditional Fresco Plaster with Pozzolana</b><br> <EOL>Traditional Fresco Plaster with Pozzolana is a ready-to-use blend of aged lime putty and well-graded, coarse sharp sand in reclosable 3.5 gal. (13.25 L) pail with a separate pouch of pozzolana. Add the pozolana prior to use to make 1:2:5 (pozzolana: lime: sand) plaster. Use for the scratch coat of fresco paintings. Coverage is about 18 sq. ft. (1.67 m2) when applied 1/4 inch (6 mm) thick. Cured color is beige. One year shelf life. All natural and aged at least 30 days.",,999998,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8731,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Vehicles & Mediums/Fresco Plasters,,85.670,,Tuesday 16 November 2010 05:53:39 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,72,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53833,NAP-550-SPTG1K,bhavesh,Traditional Silverpoint (1 Kg) Ground (2.2 lb) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Traditional Silverpoint (1 Kg) Ground(2.2 lb) Bag by Natural Pigments,2.200,26,26,,* Traditional Silverpoint (1 Kg) Ground (2.2 lb) Bag<br /> <EOL>* Traditional Silverpoint Ground is a ready-to-use dry mix ground based on Cennino Cennini’s 15th century recipe that provides the right abrasive surface for silver and other metal point drawing that is applied to paper or wood.<br /> <EOL>* Mix with an equal amount of water and warm until it is liquid enough to apply with a brush.,,999993,4,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8579,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Drawing Tools and Supplies/Sliver Point Bags,,23.430,,Monday 08 November 2010 10:44:52 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,19.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
53832,NAP-550-SPTG50,bhavesh,Traditional Silverpoint (500 g) Ground (1.1 lb) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Traditional Silverpoint (500 g) Ground(1.1 lb) Bag by Natural Pigments,1.100,14.500,14.500,,* Traditional Silverpoint (500 g) Ground(1.1 lb) Bag<br /> <EOL>* Traditional Silverpoint Ground is a ready-to-use dry mix ground based on Cennino Cennini’s 15th century recipe that provides the right abrasive surface for silver and other metal point drawing that is applied to paper or wood.<br /> <EOL>* Mix with an equal amount of water and warm until it is liquid enough to apply with a brush.<br /> <EOL>,,999994,6,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,57728,Painting and Painting Accessories/Raw Materials/Pigments,,14.670,,Monday 08 November 2010 10:40:05 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,10.880,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58564,NAP-681-16522,bhavesh2,Utility Scrub Brush: 8",Utility Scrub Brush: 8",0.500,5.600,5.600,,<B>Utility Scrub Brush: 8"</b><BR><BR> <EOL><b>About Utility Scrub Brush</b><BR> <EOL>The short handle brush is great for cleaning surfaces and tools. White tampico bristles are set in a high-tensile strength foam plastic block. The scrub brush will not absorb water and is made for long service.,,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8932,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Tools,,7.610,,Monday 13 December 2010 07:10:45 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,5.600,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55183,NAP-510-41OVX08,bhavesh,Vacuum-Bodied (Extra High Viscosity) Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Vacuum-Bodied (Extra High Viscosity) Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle,0.500,9.500,9.500,,"Vacuum-Bodied (Extra High Viscosity) Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle<BR><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><BR> <EOL>* Natural Source: Linseed Linum usitatissimum<bR> <EOL>* Acid Value (mg KOH/g), max: 2.2 <br> <EOL>* Color (Gardner): 4<br> <EOL>* Iodine Value: - <br> <EOL>* Viscosity (Stokes @ 25° C): 208<br> <EOL>* Appearance: Clear/Transparent at 25° C<br> <EOL>* Specific gravity: 0.960 @ 25° C<br> <EOL>* Weight Per Gallon: 8.03 lbs.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Vacuum-Bodied Oil</b><BR> <EOL>Stand oil is is heat treated and polymerized (thickened) oil. This heat-bodied oil is made from well-refined linseed oil from American flax seeds that is cooked in vacuum-kettles. Vacuum-bodied oils have a lower acid value, better color and yellows less than bodied oils obtained by conventional open-kettle cooking and unbodied oils. <EOL><br><<BR> <EOL>This vacuum-bodied linseed oil has a low acid value, low viscosity and is light colored. It is a stand oil that gives gloss, brushabilty and non-yellowing characteristics when compared to other stand or bodied oils. Bodied oils form harder films than raw or refined linseed oil. <EOL><Br><br> <EOL>The term ""stand oil"" is derived from the Dutch word that designated a drying oil heat treated and aged by standing in tanks. Later it applied to oils that were bodied by heat treating for prolonged periods in open kettles. Stand oil, invented in the 19th century, replaced Venice turpentine and sun-thickened linseed oil in artists' painting mediums. Stand oil leaves an enamel-like finish to paint. Bodied oils form harder films and yellow less than refined or raw linseed oils. The use of the term ""stand oil"" is antiquated since bodied oils today are processed differently than those in the 19th century. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Adding large amounts of bodied oil may increase the tendency of oil paint to wrinkle (alligator). Adding as little as 10% by volume of bodied oil to painting mediums increases the viscosity of the medium and slows down the drying time. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>Use turpentine, spike oil or mineral spirits as the solvent for bodied oils and for brush and studio clean up. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>Warning:</b><br> Rags or paper towels contaminated with vegetable drying oils, particularly those containing iron oxide pigments are susceptible to spontaneous combustion. To prevent unexpected fires, used rags or paper towels contaminated with oil-based materials should be collected in a closeable, air-tight container. Store water-dampened rags or paper towels in a metal container with an air-tight top. Alternately, washing contaminated rags will remove contaminating materials and eliminate risk. <EOL>",,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,50263,Furniture for Artists/Lamps and Lighting,,9.690,,Tuesday 16 November 2010 10:51:11 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,7.130,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55182,NAP-510-41OVT08,bhavesh,Vacuum-Bodied (High Viscosity) Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Vacuum-Bodied (High Viscosity) Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle,0.500,9.500,9.500,,"Vacuum-Bodied (High Viscosity) Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle<BR><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><BR> <EOL>* Natural Source: Linseed Linum usitatissimum<bR> <EOL>* Acid Value (mg KOH/g), max: 2.7 <br> <EOL>* Color (Gardner): 3<br> <EOL>* Iodine Value: - <br> <EOL>* Viscosity (Stokes @ 25° C): 73<br> <EOL>* Appearance: Clear/Transparent at 25° C<br> <EOL>* Specific gravity: 0.960 @ 25° C<br> <EOL>* Weight Per Gallon: 8.00 lbs.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Vacuum-Bodied Oil</b><BR> <EOL>Stand oil is is heat treated and polymerized (thickened) oil. This heat-bodied oil is made from well-refined linseed oil from American flax seeds that is cooked in vacuum-kettles. Vacuum-bodied oils have a lower acid value, better color and yellows less than bodied oils obtained by conventional open-kettle cooking and unbodied oils. <EOL><br><<BR> <EOL>This vacuum-bodied linseed oil has a low acid value, low viscosity and is light colored. It is a stand oil that gives gloss, brushabilty and non-yellowing characteristics when compared to other stand or bodied oils. Bodied oils form harder films than raw or refined linseed oil. <EOL><Br><br> <EOL>The term ""stand oil"" is derived from the Dutch word that designated a drying oil heat treated and aged by standing in tanks. Later it applied to oils that were bodied by heat treating for prolonged periods in open kettles. Stand oil, invented in the 19th century, replaced Venice turpentine and sun-thickened linseed oil in artists' painting mediums. Stand oil leaves an enamel-like finish to paint. Bodied oils form harder films and yellow less than refined or raw linseed oils. The use of the term ""stand oil"" is antiquated since bodied oils today are processed differently than those in the 19th century. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Adding large amounts of bodied oil may increase the tendency of oil paint to wrinkle (alligator). Adding as little as 10% by volume of bodied oil to painting mediums increases the viscosity of the medium and slows down the drying time. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>Use turpentine, spike oil or mineral spirits as the solvent for bodied oils and for brush and studio clean up. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>Warning:</b><br> Rags or paper towels contaminated with vegetable drying oils, particularly those containing iron oxide pigments are susceptible to spontaneous combustion. To prevent unexpected fires, used rags or paper towels contaminated with oil-based materials should be collected in a closeable, air-tight container. Store water-dampened rags or paper towels in a metal container with an air-tight top. Alternately, washing contaminated rags will remove contaminating materials and eliminate risk. <EOL>",,999997,3,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8727,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Vehicles & Mediums/Oils,,9.690,,Tuesday 16 November 2010 10:47:23 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,7.130,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55179,NAP-510-41OVL08,bhavesh,Vacuum-Bodied (Low Viscosity) Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Vacuum-Bodied (Low Viscosity) Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle,0.500,9.500,9.500,,"Vacuum-Bodied (Low Viscosity) Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle<BR><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><BR> <EOL>* Natural Source: Linseed Linum usitatissimum<bR> <EOL>* Acid Value (mg KOH/g), max: 3.9 <br> <EOL>* Color (Gardner): 5 <br> <EOL>* Iodine Value: - <br> <EOL>* Viscosity (Stokes @ 25° C): 27<br> <EOL>* Appearance: Clear/Transparent at 25° C<br> <EOL>* Specific gravity: 0.960 @ 25° C<br> <EOL>* Weight Per Gallon: 8.01 lbs.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Vacuum-Bodied Oil</b><BR> <EOL>Stand oil is is heat treated and polymerized (thickened) oil. This heat-bodied oil is made from well-refined linseed oil from American flax seeds that is cooked in vacuum-kettles. Vacuum-bodied oils have a lower acid value, better color and yellows less than bodied oils obtained by conventional open-kettle cooking and unbodied oils. <EOL><br><<BR> <EOL>This vacuum-bodied linseed oil has a low acid value, low viscosity and is light colored. It is a stand oil that gives gloss, brushabilty and non-yellowing characteristics when compared to other stand or bodied oils. Bodied oils form harder films than raw or refined linseed oil. <EOL><Br><br> <EOL>The term ""stand oil"" is derived from the Dutch word that designated a drying oil heat treated and aged by standing in tanks. Later it applied to oils that were bodied by heat treating for prolonged periods in open kettles. Stand oil, invented in the 19th century, replaced Venice turpentine and sun-thickened linseed oil in artists' painting mediums. Stand oil leaves an enamel-like finish to paint. Bodied oils form harder films and yellow less than refined or raw linseed oils. The use of the term ""stand oil"" is antiquated since bodied oils today are processed differently than those in the 19th century. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Adding large amounts of bodied oil may increase the tendency of oil paint to wrinkle (alligator). Adding as little as 10% by volume of bodied oil to painting mediums increases the viscosity of the medium and slows down the drying time. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>Use turpentine, spike oil or mineral spirits as the solvent for bodied oils and for brush and studio clean up. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Linseed oil is a yellowish drying oil derived from the dried ripe seeds of the flax plant (Linum usitatissimum, Linaceae). <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>Warning:</b><br> Rags or paper towels contaminated with vegetable drying oils, particularly those containing iron oxide pigments are susceptible to spontaneous combustion. To prevent unexpected fires, used rags or paper towels contaminated with oil-based materials should be collected in a closeable, air-tight container. Store water-dampened rags or paper towels in a metal container with an air-tight top. Alternately, washing contaminated rags will remove contaminating materials and eliminate risk. <EOL>",,1000000,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,57403,Painting and Painting Accessories/Oil Painting/Oil Painting Mediums/Linseed and Drying Oils,,12.810,,Tuesday 16 November 2010 10:32:14 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,9.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
59376,NAP-510-41OVM08,bhavesh,Vacuum-Bodied (Med. Viscosity) Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Vacuum-Bodied (Med. Viscosity) Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle,0.500,9.500,9.500,,"Vacuum-Bodied (Med. Viscosity) Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle<BR><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><BR> <EOL>* Natural Source: Linseed (Linum usitatissimum)<br> <EOL>* Acid Value (mg KOH/g): 1.9<BR> <EOL>* Color (Gardner): 3<BR> <EOL>* Viscosity (Stokes @ 25° C): 41<BR> <EOL>* Appearance: 	Clear/Transparent at 25° C<BR> <EOL>* Specific gravity: 0.960 @ 25° C<BR> <EOL>* Weight Per Gallon: 8.00 lbs.",,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8727,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Vehicles & Mediums/Oils,,9.690,,Saturday 18 December 2010 05:53:47 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,7.130,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55292,NAP-530-36008,bhavesh,Velázquez Medium 8 fl oz (236 ml) Can: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Velázquez Medium 8 fl oz (236 ml) Can by Natural Pigments,0.500,21,21,,"Velázquez Medium 8 fl oz (236 ml) Can: Made in USA by Natural Pigments<BR><br> <EOL><b>About Impasto Medium</b><Br> <EOL>Velázquez Medium is an oil painting medium of finely ground calcite in bodied linseed oil. Use it to extend paint and alter its consistency, making oil colors 'long'* for finer detail and impastos. Softer than Impasto Medium, this flowing paste makes colors slightly transparent while allowing you to build impasted, thick applications of paint. When added to oil paint it does not alter the color temperature. It can be thinned with solvent or oil. Depending upon the proportion added to paint, it does not affect the drying time significantly. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>Velázquez Medium does not contain stearates, solvents, driers or natural or synthetic resins, so it is safe to add to oil paint without the worry of cracking or delaminating. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>Long refers to the consistency of paint that displays tall peaks when a palette knife is pressed to its surface and lifted. Long paint is also described as being a ""ropy"" and refers to a stringy quality, like that of honey. Paint that behaves in this way is said to have long rheology. Short rheology refers to paint that exhibits a more buttery consistency, typical of most commercial oil paint. Rheology is the study of how substances flow, such as liquids and soft solids that flow rather than deform elastically. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL><b>Velázquez Medium is a calcite-rich oil painting medium.</b><BR> <EOL>The soft white paste has little affect on color, making them less opaque and slightly less saturated. Use it to build thick applications of paint.<Br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>Comparison of Impasto Medium (top left) and Velázquez Medium (top right) shows the different handling characteristics added to paint.</b><bR><Br> <EOL>Velázquez Medium slightly increases the transparency of colors while introducing flowout and leveling. These properties allow you to create fine detail in impasto or thick paint with ease. Although the paint becomes long when Velázquez Medium is added, it holds brushstrokes well. In the above example, when added to green earth artist oil (bottom center), the mixture of Impasto Medium (bottom left) extends the color and its consistency, while the mixture with Velázquez Medium (bottom right) gives the paint a long, ropy consistency. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL><b>Directions</b><BR> <EOL>Mix Velázquez Medium directly into your paint right on the palette. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Velázquez Medium is a great way to add calcite to your own paint. Add Velázquez Medium and linseed oil directly to pigment powder until a stiff paste is obtained (almost the consistency of putty). Grind the paste with a muller on a flat surface before storing in collapsible tube. Some of its properties will be temporarily lost when grinding Velázquez Medium with a muller, but should be restored when allowed to stand.",,999992,9,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,57402,Painting and Painting Accessories/Oil Painting/Oil Painting Mediums/Impasto Mediums and Extenders,,18.980,,Wednesday 17 November 2010 08:45:40 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,15.750,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55290,NAP-530-31008,bhavesh,Venetian Medium 4 oz (118 ml): Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Venetian Medium 4 oz (118 ml): Made in USA by Natural Pigments,0.250,35,35,,"Venetian Medium 4 oz (118 ml): Made in USA by Natural Pigments<BR><br> <EOL><b>About Venetian Medium</b><Br> <EOL>Venetian Medium is an oil-painting medium based on the research that 16th century Venetian painters added powdered glass to their paint. Venetian Medium contains leaded crystal glass powder, the palest bodied linseed oil, sun-thickened walnut oil with small amounts of wax, odorless mineral spirits and lead drier. Spread thinly onto the surface and paint directly into it as a couch or add directly to paint nut. Smooths the edges of brush or knife strokes. Venetian Medium is fast setting and dries to a satin finish. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL><b>Directions:</b><BR> Spread thinly onto the surface and paint directly into it or mix directly into paint on the palette to give colors a flowing consistency that holds brush strokes yet dries to a satin finish. Use to “oil out” or as a painting couch by rubbing a thin layer onto completely dried paint. Gives paint a longer, flowing consistency. <EOL><br><br> <EOL><b>Recommendation:</b><BR> To prevent Venetian Medium from skinning in the can while in storage, add a small amount of linseed oil, covering the surface of the medium. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL><b>WARNING!</b><br> <EOL> CONTAINS LEAD AND MINERAL SPIRITS. Do not take internally. Avoid eye and skin contact. Avoid long exposure by inhalation. Use with adequate ventilation. KEEP OUT OF REACH OF CHILDREN AND PETS. Conforms to ASTM D 4236 health requirements.",,999999,2,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8737,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Vehicles & Mediums/Mix Mediums,,45.330,,Wednesday 17 November 2010 08:34:14 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,35,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58561,NAP-681-16062,bhavesh2,Venetian Plastering Trowel: 8 3/4" X 3 3/4",Venetian Plastering Trowel: 8 3/4" X 3 3/4",0.500,40,40,,"<B>Venetian Plastering Trowel: 8 3/4"" X 3 3/4""</b><BR><BR> <EOL><b>About Venetian Plastering Trowel</b><BR> <EOL>Venetian plastering trowels are used in finishing the surface of the plaster to the required smoothness and are ideal for achieving the highly polished ""Venetian"" look. Troweling represents the last stage in the finishing process of the plaster. This action helps compact the surface and adds to the quality and durability of the work.<BR><BR> <EOL>This finishing trowel has a stainless steel blade with beveled edges and radius corners, and the blade is cross-ground (usually only found on better finishing trowels) to hold its shape better. The curved, hardwood handle commonly called a California or Camel Back pattern is designed for better handling. Each handle is machine fitted onto the milled shank. Tests prove it took 30% more torque to twist a Marshalltown handle than that of the nearest competitor. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Finishing trowels are narrower and longer than plastering trowels and the blade is slightly convex. The standard width is 10 cm (4 inches) but the length may range from 30.5 to 50.8 cm (12 to 20 inches). Many finishers use a fanning pattern for the final finishing, which usually requires a narrower blade that is 7.5 to 9 cm (3 to 3-1/2 inches) wide. Ten rivets are used in the shorter trowels but as many as 16 are used in the longer sizes.",,1000000,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8932,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Tools,,51.800,,Monday 13 December 2010 07:07:17 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,40,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54679,NAP-510-10VRMD1K,bhavesh,Verona Red Marble Dust 1 kg (2.2 lbs) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Verona Red Marble Dust 1 kg (2.2 lbs) Bag by Natural Pigments,2.200,7.500,7.500,,"Verona Red Marble Dust 1 kg (2.2 lbs) Bag<BR><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><BR> <EOL>* Calcium Carbonate (Ca<sub>2</sub>CO<sub>3</sub>): 98.75%<br> <EOL>* Magnesium Carbonate (MgCo<sub>3</sub>): <1.00%<br><br> <EOL><b>Other Impurities:</b><Br> <EOL>* Manganese dioxide (MnO<sub>2</sub>): <0.25%<br> <EOL>* Hardness: 2.8<br> <EOL>* Specific Gravity: 2.7<br> <EOL>* Bulk Density: 89 lbs./ft<sup>3</sup><br> <EOL>* Dry Brightness: 98<br> <EOL>* Average Particle Size: 25 microns<br> <EOL>* Particle Size Distribution: 0-70 microns<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Verona Red Marble Ground</b><Br> <EOL>Verona Red marble ground to medium coarse powder. Use this marble dust to make grounds, for adding textural and handling qualities to paints, and as filler in lime plastic for the intonaco layer of fresco. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Imported from the world-class deposit in Italy, it is ground to a granular particle size of 0 to 0.7 mm to retain its crystalline shape. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Marble is calcite formed from limestone with heat and pressure over years in the earth's crust. The pressure causes the limestone to change the particle structure, causing it to recrystallize. Fossilized materials in the limestone, along with its original carbonate minerals, recrystallize to form large, coarse grains of calcite. <EOL>",,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8666,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Grounds/Marble Dusts,,7.660,,Saturday 13 November 2010 09:14:55 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,5.630,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54682,NAP-510-10VRMD5K,bhavesh,Verona Red Marble Dust 5 kg (11 lbs) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Verona Red Marble Dust 5 kg (11 lbs) Bag by Natural Pigments,11,30,30,,"Verona Red Marble Dust 5 kg (11 lbs) Bag<BR><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><BR> <EOL>* Calcium Carbonate (Ca<sub>2</sub>CO<sub>3</sub>): 98.75%<br> <EOL>* Magnesium Carbonate (MgCo<sub>3</sub>): <1.00%<br><br> <EOL><b>Other Impurities:</b><Br> <EOL>* Manganese dioxide (MnO<sub>2</sub>): <0.25%<br> <EOL>* Hardness: 2.8<br> <EOL>* Specific Gravity: 2.7<br> <EOL>* Bulk Density: 89 lbs./ft<sup>3</sup><br> <EOL>* Dry Brightness: 98<br> <EOL>* Average Particle Size: 25 microns<br> <EOL>* Particle Size Distribution: 0-70 microns<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Verona Red Marble Ground</b><Br> <EOL>Verona Red marble ground to medium coarse powder. Use this marble dust to make grounds, for adding textural and handling qualities to paints, and as filler in lime plastic for the intonaco layer of fresco. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Imported from the world-class deposit in Italy, it is ground to a granular particle size of 0 to 0.7 mm to retain its crystalline shape. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Marble is calcite formed from limestone with heat and pressure over years in the earth's crust. The pressure causes the limestone to change the particle structure, causing it to recrystallize. Fossilized materials in the limestone, along with its original carbonate minerals, recrystallize to form large, coarse grains of calcite. <EOL>",,999997,3,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8666,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Grounds/Marble Dusts,,26.980,,Saturday 13 November 2010 09:18:35 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,22.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54758,NAP-510-11VIC5K,bhavesh,Vicenza Earth Extender 5 kg (11 lbs) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Vicenza Earth Extender 5 kg (11 lbs) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pi###,11,80,80,,"Vicenza Earth (5 kg) (11 lbs) Bag<BR><br> <EOL><b>About Vicenza Earth</b><br> <EOL>Vicenza earth is buff white or tan-colored clay with a subtle, warm hue and low opacity. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Add Vicenza earth to gesso and chalk ground recipes to make the ground smoother for gilding and painting surfaces. Vicenza earth in paint and bole recipes to replace clay and bentonite. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Use it is a useful glazing color to impart warmth to cooler tones. It also provides a delicate cloudiness that can help to soften focus and articulate a sense of space. Use Vicenza earth with heavy pigments to prevent separation in oil paint and to give colors a short, buttery consistency. <EOL>",,999998,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8681,"Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Grounds/Terra Alba, Vicenza Earth & White Kaolinite with Bags",,71.440,,Monday 15 November 2010 04:56:26 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,60,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55243,NAP-510-43ORW08,bhavesh,Walnut Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Walnut Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,0.500,10.500,10.500,,"Walnut Oil 8 oz (237 ml) Bottle<BR><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><BR> <EOL>* Source: Juglans regia<br> <EOL>* Linoleic Acid: 59.6%<br> <EOL>* Linolenic Acid: 13.5%<br> <EOL>* Oleic Acid: 16.2%<br> <EOL>* Palmitic Acid: 7.3%<br> <EOL>* Stearic Acid: 2.5%<br> <EOL>* Iodine Value: 151.89<br> <EOL>* Refractive Index: 1.4692<br> <EOL>* Color (Lovibond): 7Y/1.0R<br> <EOL>* Specific gravity: 0.924–0.927 @ 15° C<BR> <EOL>* Drying Index: 86.6<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Walnut Oil</b><BR>  <EOL>Our walnut oil is is cold-pressed from freshly dried walnuts (Juglans regia), and then lightly refined. It is a clear, pale yellow oil that has a distinctive odor. As a thin oil, it is used to make oil paint more fluid. As it yellows less than linseed oil (but more than safflower oil) it is good for making pale oil colors. Walnut oil dries more slowly than linseed oil, drying in four or five days. It is said to have a less tendency to crack than linseed oil. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>As early as the fifth century walnut oil was recommended by Aetius for varnishing wax pictures and gilt surfaces. It is recommended for all light pigments in the treatises on painting by Leonardo da Vinci, Vasari, Borghini, Lornazzo, Armenini, Bisagno, Volpato, and others. <EOL><br><bR> <EOL>Must be stored in a cool, dry place away from direct light. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL><b>Warning:</b> Read carefully cautions from the label of this product.",,999996,3,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8727,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Vehicles & Mediums/Oils,,10.630,,Wednesday 17 November 2010 07:03:43 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,7.880,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54188,NAP-301-1101,bhavesh,Water Gilding Kit Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Water Gilding Kit Made in USA by Natural Pigments,0.250,243.390,243.390,,"* The Aurum Gilding Arts Water Gilding Kit has all the tools and supplies you need to complete a water gilding project from start to finish.<br /> <EOL>* Included are the materials to apply the gilding base or bole; cut, handle and apply gold leaf; and polish the gold.<br /><br> <EOL><b> The complete kit includes:</b><br /> <EOL>* 1 each Gilders' Cushion<br> <EOL>* 1 each Gilders' Knife<br> <EOL>* 1 each Gilders' Agate Burnisher<br> <EOL>* 1 each Reed Breathing Tube<br> <EOL>* 1 each Gilders' Tip<br> <EOL>* 1 each Mop Brush<br> <EOL>* 1 each Round Squirrel Brush<br> <EOL>* 1 each Gold Leaf, 23.5 Karat, book<br> <EOL>* 1 each LeFranc & Bourgeois Charbonnel Gilders' Clay, net vol 4 oz<br> <EOL>* 1 each Italian Rabbit Skin Glue, net vol 4 oz<br> <EOL>* Steel Wool Pads, Cotton Balls and Stirring Sticks<br> <EOL>* Practical Gilding<br> <EOL>",,0,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,299.760,,Thursday 11 November 2010 05:24:45 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,243.390,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58351,NAP-624-209212F,bhavesh,Watercolor Case with 12 Full Pans,Watercolor Case with 12 Full Pans,0.500,88.800,88.800,,"<B>Watercolor Case with 12 Full Pans</b><BR> <EOL><B>About Watercolor Case</b><BR> <EOL>This Rublev Watercolor Case is ideal for the traveling watercolor artist. It features 12 full (empty) pans with an integral fold out lid that has four paint wells and a separate fold out flat palette that makes mixing colors on-the-go very convenient. There is 21 cm (8.375"") long space in the center for brushes and other accessories. The case is made of heavy-gauge metal with black and white enamel. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>There is also a handy metal loop on the back that allows you to place the case on your belt loop or hold it securely in hand while painting. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>You can use this case with moist watercolors in tubes or semi-moist watercolors in pans. To use the case with tube watercolors, simply fill the empty pans with tube watercolor paint and let dry. Insert the watercolor pans into the case. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Rublev semi-moist watercolors in pans easily re-wet, while some other brands do not. Simply insert the pans into the empty case. Winsor & Newton full pan watercolors also fit this case. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Overall size: 8.5"" x 2.5"" x 0.875"" (22 cm x 7 cm x 2.5 cm) (closed).<BR> <EOL>8.5"" x 8"" (22 cm x 21 cm) (fully open)<BR> <EOL>Includes 12 full or 24 half pans (empty)<BR> <EOL>Imported from Germany",,999999,6,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8932,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Tools,,113.110,,Saturday 11 December 2010 07:29:56 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,88.800,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58349,NAP-624-2091,rommel,Watercolor Case with 16 Half Pans,Watercolor Case with 16 Half Pans,0.500,66.450,66.450,,"<B>Watercolor Case with 16 Half Pans</b><BR> <EOL><B>About Watercolor Case</b><BR> <EOL>This Rublev Watercolor Case is ideal for the traveling watercolor artist. It features 16 half (empty) pans with an integral fold out lid that has three paint wells and a separate fold out flat palette that makes mixing colors on-the-go very convenient. There is 14 cm (5.5"") long space in the center for brushes and other accessories. The case is made of heavy-gauge metal with black and white enamel. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>There is also a handy metal loop on the back that allows you to place the case on your belt loop or hold it securely in hand while painting. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>You can use this case with moist watercolors in tubes or semi-moist watercolors in pans. To use the case with tube watercolors, simply fill the empty pans with tube watercolor paint and let dry. Insert the watercolor pans into the case. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Rublev semi-moist watercolors in pans easily re-wet, while some other brands do not. Simply insert the pans into the empty case. Winsor & Newton full pan watercolors also fit this case. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Overall size: 14,3 cm × 7 cm × 2,5 cm (5.5"" × 2.75"" × 1"") closed. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Includes 16 half pans (empty) <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Imported from Italy",,1000000,2,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,69.110,,Saturday 11 December 2010 07:25:41 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,49.840,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58346,NAP-624-2083,rommel,Watercolor Case with 8 Half Pans,Watercolor Case with 8 Half Pans,0.100,37.450,37.450,,"<B>Watercolor Case with 8 Half Pans</b><BR> <EOL><B>About Watercolor Case</b><BR> <EOL>This Rublev Watercolor Case is ideal for the traveling watercolor artist. It features 8 half (empty) pans with an integral fold out lid that has two paint wells and a separate fold out flat palette that makes mixing colors on-the-go very convenient. The case is made of heavy-gauge metal with black and white enamel. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>There is also a handy metal loop on the back that allows you to place the case on your belt loop or hold it securely in hand while painting. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>You can use this case with moist watercolors in tubes or semi-moist watercolors in pans. To use the case with tube watercolors, simply fill the empty pans with tube watercolor paint and let dry. Insert the watercolor pans into the case. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Rublev semi-moist watercolors in pans easily re-wet, while some other brands do not. Simply insert the pans into the empty case. Winsor & Newton half pan watercolors also fit this case. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Overall size: 8,2 cm × 6,2 cm × 1,5 cm (3.25"" × 2.5"" × 0.625"") closed. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Includes 8 half pans (empty) <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Imported from Italy",,1000000,1,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,36.390,,Saturday 11 December 2010 07:15:06 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,28.090,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55271,NAP-510-5508,bhavesh,Watercolor Medium 8 fl oz (237 ml) Bottle: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Watercolor Medium 8 fl oz (237 ml) Bottle by Natural Pigments,0.500,12.990,12.990,,"Watercolor Medium 8 fl oz (237 ml) Bottle<BR><br> <EOL><b>About Watercolor Medium</b><Br> <EOL>Natural Pigments Watercolor Medium is a solution of gum arabic, honey and a small amount of preservative to make your own watercolors. Maintains watercolor's transparency and brilliance. Use it to increase watercolor transparency and brightness or to improve adhesion and spread the brush stroke. Mix with dry pigments to provide a smooth, water-soluble paste with a honey-like consistency. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>This is the basic medium we use in our own watercolor paints. Disperse pigments in this medium by placing a small amount in a pile of dry powder pigment and then mull to creamy smoothness. Also use watercolor medium to dilute dried watercolor paint. Works well with any watercolors. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>Note: Best if stored in a refrigerator. Store away from light in a cool location. <EOL>",,999999,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8737,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Vehicles & Mediums/Mix Mediums,,13.130,,Wednesday 17 November 2010 07:51:10 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,9.740,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58222,NAP-601-1104,bhavesh,"Watercolor Paint Making Kit, Made in USA by Natural Pigments","Watercolor Paint Making Kit, Made in USA by Natural Pigments",1,137,137,,"<B>Watercolor Paint Making Kit</b><BR><BR> <EOL><B>About Watercolor Paint Making Kit</b><BR> <EOL>The Natural Pigments Watercolor Paint Making Kit is intended for artists who want to expand their painting horizons, but have little or no experience making their own watercolor and/or gouache paints. The kit comes wih all the materials that you need to get started, including instructions, glass muller, grinding surface and six traditional pigments in dry powder form to start making your own watercolor or gouache paint. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>It is an excellent introduction to paint making, which can open the door to a new range of possibilities in different mediums, pigments and paint recipes. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL><B>The kit includes the following items: </b><BR> <EOL>* 1 each Introductory Pigment Sampler<BR> <EOL>* 1 each Muller, glass Large<BR> <EOL>* 1 each Grinding surface, 254 x 254 x 63 mm (10 x 10 x 0.25 in.) tempered glass, not sendblasted<BR> <EOL>* 1 each Spatula<BR> <EOL>* 1 each Dispenser Bottle<BR> <EOL>* 1 each Silicon carbide, 100 grit, net dry vol. 1 oz. (29 cc) jar<BR> <EOL>* 1 each Watercolor Medium, 8 fl oz (232 ml)<BR> <EOL>* 6 each Collapsible Metal Tubes and Caps, lacquered, 20 ml<BR> <EOL>* 1 each Making Watercolor Colors: containing instructions for preparing the grinding surface and making your own water-borne watercolor paint (sent by PDF)<BR><BR> <EOL><B>Pigments Included in the Kit</b><BR> <EOL>The kit includes one ounce (29 ml) each of Glauconite, Umber, Titanium White, Gold Ochre, Red Ochre, and German black -- all packaged in individual plastic jars. These pigments represent a basic set of hues used in historical painting before the 19th century.<BR><BR> <EOL><B>Purpose of the Watercolor Paint-Making Kit</b><BR> <EOL>The Natural Pigments Watercolor Paint-Making Kit is designed for artists who wish to make small amounts of watercolor paint. You will find it useful for making paint on the spot, as you need them. Unlike larger grinding tools, the small size of these tools allows for easy carefree cleanup between use. It's also a great educational tool for instructors to demonstrate how artists' paint was made prior to the 19th century.",,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,10,Y,8932,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Tools,,122.130,,Friday 10 December 2010 07:51:20 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,102.750,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58348,NAP-624-2086,rommel,Watercolor Travel Case with 8 Half Pans,Watercolor Travel Case with 8 Half Pans,0.500,69.950,69.950,,"<B>Watercolor Travel Case with 8 Half Pans</b><BR> <EOL><B>About Watercolor Travel Case</b><BR> <EOL>This Rublev Watercolor Travel Case is ideal for the traveling watercolor artist. It features 8 half (empty) pans with an integral water bottle, cup and a convenient fold-out palette. The case is made of heavy-gauge metal with black and white enamel. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>There is also a handy metal loop on the back that allows you to place the case on your belt loop or hold it securely in hand while painting. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>You can use this case with moist watercolors in tubes or semi-moist watercolors in pans. To use the case with tube watercolors, simply fill the empty pans with tube watercolor paint and let dry. Insert the watercolor pans into the case. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Rublev semi-moist watercolors in pans easily re-wet, while some other brands do not. Simply insert the pans into the empty case. Winsor & Newton half pan watercolors also fit this case. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Overall size: 9,7 cm × 6,2 cm × 2,5 cm (3.75"" × 2.5"" × 1"") closed. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Includes 12 half pans (empty) <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Imported from Italy",,1000000,3,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8932,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Tools,,120.450,,Saturday 11 December 2010 07:20:33 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,69.950,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55339,NAP-540-5416,bhavesh,Wax Medium 473 ml (16 fl oz): Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Wax Medium 473 ml (16 fl oz): Made in USA by Natural Pigments,1,18.500,18.500,,"Wax Medium 473 ml (16 fl oz)<BR><br> <EOL><b>About Wax Medium</b><Br> <EOL>Natural Pigments Wax Medium is blend of naturally bleached beeswax, Carnauba wax and damar resin in a soft paste. This blend produces a harder film and more shine than wax or wax paste alone. It is a soft paste formulated to make oil colors thicker. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Wax Medium gives a satin finish to colors, yet does not extend the drying time of oil paint, making it thicker and more workable. Add to oil colors as a working medium to add body to paint. When making your own oil colors add wax medium to oil when grinding pigments. The wax helps to give the paint a buttery consistency and guards against oil separating from pigment. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Natural Pigments Wax Medium can be used in a painting technique called ""encaustic."" To make a encaustic paint moisten pigment with mineral spirits or turpentine to form a paste. Add wax medium to the pigment paste until the desired consistency is reached.",,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,57407,Painting and Painting Accessories/Oil Painting/Oil Painting Mediums/Wax Mediums,,18.570,,Wednesday 17 November 2010 10:31:53 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,13.880,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55332,NAP540-5316,bhavesh,Wax Paste 473 ml (16 fl oz): Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Wax Paste 473 ml (16 fl oz): Made in USA by Natural Pigments,1,15.500,15.500,,"Wax Paste 473 ml (16 fl oz)<BR><br> <EOL><b>About Oleogel </b><Br> <EOL>Natural Pigments Wax Paste is made with beeswax and odorless mineral spirits. It is a soft paste formulated to make oil colors thicker and more matte. It can also be used as a final varnish over a dry painting or mixed with varnish to reduce gloss. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>Natural Pigments Wax Paste cuts the glossy appearance of oil paints, giving them a more satin finish while extending the drying time of paints, making them thicker and more workable for longer periods of time. When making your own oil colors you may add wax paste to oil when grinding pigments. The wax helps to give the paint a buttery consistency and guards against oil separating from pigment. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Natural Pigments Wax Paste can be used as a protective coating (varnish) over a painting, as a paint binder, and as a stabilizer in oil colors. It melts between 62°–65° C. (144°–149° F.) and dissolves when heated in turpentine, mineral spirits or oil. It does not darken or change color with age, and it resists the action of atmospheric impurities more than do resins or oils. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Natural Pigments Wax Paste can be used in a painting technique called ""encaustic."" To make a encaustic paint moisten pigment with mineral spirits or turpentine to form a paste. Add wax medium to the pigment paste until desired consistency is reached.",,1000000,5,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8726,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Vehicles & Mediums/Waxes,,15.680,,Wednesday 17 November 2010 10:20:51 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,11.630,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55089,NAP-510-33WAX10,bhavesh,White Beeswax 1 kg (Prills) 2.2 lb Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,White Beeswax 1 kg (Prills) 2.2 lb Bag by Natural Pigments,2.200,29.500,29.500,,"White Beeswax 1 kg (Prills) 2.2 lb Bag<BR><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><BR> <EOL>* Source: Apis mellifera<br> <EOL>* Synonyms: White Beeswax, Cera Alba, White Wax, Cire Blanche, Weisses Wachs, Cera blanca<br> <EOL>* Appearance: White<br> <EOL>* Acid Value: 19.5<br> <EOL>* Ester Value: 73.4<br> <EOL>* Melting Point: 65° C. (149° F.)<br> <EOL>* Refractive Index: 1.438–1.442 <br> <EOL>* Specific gravity: 0.966–0.973 @ 25° C<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>About White Beeswax (Prills)</b><BR> <EOL> <EOL>These prills of white beeswax derived from a natural source, bee apiaries in North America, that is naturally bleached to a soft, pleasing white color. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>Beeswax is used as a protective coating (varnish) in painting, as a paint binder, and as a stabilizer in oil colors. It is usually available in the form of cakes, pastilles or prills, either bleached white or in its natural yellowish color. It melts between 62°–65° C. (144°–149° F.) and will dissolve when heated in water, turpentine, mineral spirits, or oil. Beeswax does not oxidize and polymerize as does drying oil, but rather, solidifies as it cools to make an solid mass. It does not darken or change color with age, and it resists the action of atmospheric impurities more than do resins or oils. On the other hand, it is somewhat more sensitive to temperature changes, becoming soft in heat and brittle in cold. It is also more sensitive to abrasion and rubbing than a dried film of oil or varnish. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>White beeswax is the recommended choice for most painting techniques calling for wax ingredients. Beeswax cuts the glossy quality of oil paints, giving them a more satin finish while extending the drying time of paints, making them thicker and more workable for longer periods of time. When making your own oil colors you may add about 2% white beeswax when grinding colors. The wax helps to give the paint a more buttery consistency and guards against flocculation of the pigment. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>Beeswax is used in a painting technique called ""encaustic."" The technique itself is very simple. Pigment is added to molten beeswax and often resin (such as Venice turpentine or damar), which is then applied hot to the painting surface. The surface itself may be warmed allowing for manipulation of the encaustic paint. It may also be cool causing the brush stroke to immediately solidify. The final treatment is the ""burning in"" which consists of passing a heat source over the surface, fusing and bonding the painting. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL><b>Origin and History</B><BR> <EOL>The English term wax is derived from the Anglo-Saxon word weax for beeswax, so a practical definition of a wax may therefore be a substance similar in composition and physical properties to beeswax. Technologists use the term for a variety of commercial products of mineral, marine, plant and insect origin that contain fatty materials of various kinds. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Beeswax is the oldest known pigment binder. Since ancient Greece, beeswax was first used in painting by heating it over a charcoal pot, hence the term encaustic, literally meaning burning in. The Egyptians, Greeks, and Romans would melt a mixture of beeswax and often resin over this heat-source, blending the ingredients together. Once the wax melted pigments were introduced into the mixture. The wax color was then painted onto a wooden support using natural hair brushes or heated metal tools. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL><b>Source</b><br> <EOL>Glands under the abdomen of bees secrete a wax, which they use to construct honeycombs. Beeswax in the honeycomb form is familiar to everyone. When the honey is extracted, a crude yellow wax remains that can be melted and filtered. It contains a high proportion of wax esters (35 to 80%). The hydrocarbon content is highly variable, and may be altered somewhat as beekeepers may feed some to bees to improve the yield of honey. This crude wax is a yellowish-brown solid; somewhat brittle when cold, but becoming plastic by the heat of the hand. It has an agreeable, honey-like odor. The color varies depending upon the impurities collected with the wax during its harvest. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>The color of yellow wax is bleached by exposing it, with an extended surface, to the combined influence of air, light and moisture. When yellow beeswax is melted, formed into thin sheets, and exposed to sunlight and air, it becomes white. In a few days the sheets are partially bleached; but, to deprive the wax completely of color, it is often necessary to repeat the whole process. When sufficiently white, it is melted and cast into cakes. Yellow wax may also be decolorized by treatment with charcoal or with potassium permanganate, potassium dichromate and sulfuric acid, and hydrogen peroxide. The bleaching process raises the melting point of the wax. Because it is bleached, white beeswax is the recommended choice for most painting techniques calling for wax ingredients. White beeswax is less unctuous to the touch than yellow; it is soft and ductile at 35° C. (95° F.) and fusible at 65° C. (149° F.), retaining its fluidity at a lower temperature. <EOL>",,1000000,2,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8726,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Vehicles & Mediums/Waxes,,29.500,,Tuesday 16 November 2010 08:06:26 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,22.130,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55103,NAP-510-33WAX05,bhavesh,White Beeswax 500 g (Prills) 1.1 lb Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,White Beeswax 500 g (Prills) 1.1 lb Bag by Natural Pigments,1.100,16.500,16.500,,"White Beeswax 500 g (Prills) 1.1 lb Bag<BR><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><BR> <EOL>* Source: Apis mellifera<br> <EOL>* Synonyms: White Beeswax, Cera Alba, White Wax, Cire Blanche, Weisses Wachs, Cera blanca<br> <EOL>* Appearance: White<br> <EOL>* Acid Value: 19.5<br> <EOL>* Ester Value: 73.4<br> <EOL>* Melting Point: 65° C. (149° F.)<br> <EOL>* Refractive Index: 1.438–1.442 <br> <EOL>* Specific gravity: 0.966–0.973 @ 25° C<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>About White Beeswax (Prills)</b><BR> <EOL> <EOL>These prills of white beeswax derived from a natural source, bee apiaries in North America, that is naturally bleached to a soft, pleasing white color. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>Beeswax is used as a protective coating (varnish) in painting, as a paint binder, and as a stabilizer in oil colors. It is usually available in the form of cakes, pastilles or prills, either bleached white or in its natural yellowish color. It melts between 62°–65° C. (144°–149° F.) and will dissolve when heated in water, turpentine, mineral spirits, or oil. Beeswax does not oxidize and polymerize as does drying oil, but rather, solidifies as it cools to make an solid mass. It does not darken or change color with age, and it resists the action of atmospheric impurities more than do resins or oils. On the other hand, it is somewhat more sensitive to temperature changes, becoming soft in heat and brittle in cold. It is also more sensitive to abrasion and rubbing than a dried film of oil or varnish. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>White beeswax is the recommended choice for most painting techniques calling for wax ingredients. Beeswax cuts the glossy quality of oil paints, giving them a more satin finish while extending the drying time of paints, making them thicker and more workable for longer periods of time. When making your own oil colors you may add about 2% white beeswax when grinding colors. The wax helps to give the paint a more buttery consistency and guards against flocculation of the pigment. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>Beeswax is used in a painting technique called ""encaustic."" The technique itself is very simple. Pigment is added to molten beeswax and often resin (such as Venice turpentine or damar), which is then applied hot to the painting surface. The surface itself may be warmed allowing for manipulation of the encaustic paint. It may also be cool causing the brush stroke to immediately solidify. The final treatment is the ""burning in"" which consists of passing a heat source over the surface, fusing and bonding the painting. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL><b>Origin and History</B><BR> <EOL>The English term wax is derived from the Anglo-Saxon word weax for beeswax, so a practical definition of a wax may therefore be a substance similar in composition and physical properties to beeswax. Technologists use the term for a variety of commercial products of mineral, marine, plant and insect origin that contain fatty materials of various kinds. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Beeswax is the oldest known pigment binder. Since ancient Greece, beeswax was first used in painting by heating it over a charcoal pot, hence the term encaustic, literally meaning burning in. The Egyptians, Greeks, and Romans would melt a mixture of beeswax and often resin over this heat-source, blending the ingredients together. Once the wax melted pigments were introduced into the mixture. The wax color was then painted onto a wooden support using natural hair brushes or heated metal tools. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL><b>Source</b><br> <EOL>Glands under the abdomen of bees secrete a wax, which they use to construct honeycombs. Beeswax in the honeycomb form is familiar to everyone. When the honey is extracted, a crude yellow wax remains that can be melted and filtered. It contains a high proportion of wax esters (35 to 80%). The hydrocarbon content is highly variable, and may be altered somewhat as beekeepers may feed some to bees to improve the yield of honey. This crude wax is a yellowish-brown solid; somewhat brittle when cold, but becoming plastic by the heat of the hand. It has an agreeable, honey-like odor. The color varies depending upon the impurities collected with the wax during its harvest. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>The color of yellow wax is bleached by exposing it, with an extended surface, to the combined influence of air, light and moisture. When yellow beeswax is melted, formed into thin sheets, and exposed to sunlight and air, it becomes white. In a few days the sheets are partially bleached; but, to deprive the wax completely of color, it is often necessary to repeat the whole process. When sufficiently white, it is melted and cast into cakes. Yellow wax may also be decolorized by treatment with charcoal or with potassium permanganate, potassium dichromate and sulfuric acid, and hydrogen peroxide. The bleaching process raises the melting point of the wax. Because it is bleached, white beeswax is the recommended choice for most painting techniques calling for wax ingredients. White beeswax is less unctuous to the touch than yellow; it is soft and ductile at 35° C. (95° F.) and fusible at 65° C. (149° F.), retaining its fluidity at a lower temperature. <EOL>",,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8726,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Vehicles & Mediums/Waxes,,16.560,,Tuesday 16 November 2010 08:13:49 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,12.380,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54738,NAP-510-15KLN1K,bhavesh2,White Kaolinite 1 kg (2.2 lbs) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,White Kaolinite 1 kg (2.2 lbs) Bag by Natural Pigments,2.200,6.850,6.850,,"White Kaolinite 1 kg (2.2 lbs) Bag<BR><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><BR> <EOL><b>Physical Properties</b><BR> <EOL>* Median Particle Size (microns): 1.5<br> <EOL>* Hegman Grind: 5.5<br> <EOL>* Residue 325 Mesh (%) (ASTM C 325-81 or C 371-77): 	0.05<br> <EOL>* Specific Gravity (ASTM C-329-75): 2.58<br><br> <EOL><b>Bulk Density:</b><br> <EOL>* Loose (lbs/cu ft): 23<br> <EOL>* Compacted (lbs/cu ft): 33<br> <EOL>* Mohs Hardness: 2.0-2.5<br> <EOL>* Oil Absorption (Gardner-Coleman): 60 g<br> <EOL>* pH Value (ASTM D 1208-78): 6.0<br> <EOL>* Brightness (Colorimeter): 	89<bR> <EOL>* Color: White<br> <EOL>* Refractive Index: 1.62<br> <EOL>* Moisture Content (max. %) (ASTM C 323-56 or C 234-82): 0.4<br> <EOL>* Loss on Ignition (%) (ASTM C 323-56): 0.3<br><br> <EOL><b>Chemical Analysis</b><br> <EOL>* Chemical Formula: Al<sub>2</sub>Si<sub>2</sub>O<sub>5</sub>(OH)<sub>4</sub><br> <EOL>* Silicon Dioxide (SiO<sub>2</sub>): 57.00%<br> <EOL>* Aluminum Oxide (Al<sub>2</sub>OS<ub>3</sub>): 39.00%<br> <EOL>* Iron Oxide (Fe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>): 1.00%<br> <EOL>* Titanium Dioxide (TiO<sub>2</sub>): 0.70%<br> <EOL>* Calcium Oxide (CaO) + Magnesium Oxide (MgO): 0.35%<br> <EOL>* Potassium Oxide (K<sub>2</sub>O) + Sodium Oxide (Na<sub>2</sub>O): 1.70%<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Kaolinite </b><br> <EOL>Kaolinite is a clay mineral with the chemical composition Al2Si2O5(OH)4. It is a layered silicate mineral, also known as china clay or kaolin. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL><b>Source</b><BR> <EOL>The name is derived from Gaoling or Kao-Ling (""High Hill"") in Jingdezhen, Jiangxi province, China. Kaolinite was first described as a mineral species in 1867 for an occurrence in the Jari River basin of Brazil. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>Kaolinite is one of the most common minerals on earth. It is mined, as kaolin, in Brazil, France, United Kingdom, Germany, India, Australia, Korea , the People's Republic of China and the USA. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Kaolinite is a soft, earthy, usually white mineral, produced by the chemical weathering of aluminum silicate minerals like feldspar. In many parts of the world, it is colored pink-orange-red by iron oxide, giving it a distinct rust hue. Lighter concentrations of iron oxide yield white, yellow or light orange colors. Alternating layers of colored clay are sometimes found, as at Providence Canyon State Park in Georgia, USA. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Our white kaolin clay is from deposits in Texas, USA and is heat treated to remove some portion of its hydroxyl (OH) composition. Calcined kaolin is produced by heating ultrafine natural kaolinite to high temperatures in a kiln. The calcination process increases whiteness and hardness and alters the size and shape of the kaolin particles. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Kaolin-type clays undergo a series of transformations upon heating in air at atmospheric pressure. Dehydration begins at 550-600° C to produce disordered metakaolin, Al2Si2O7, but continuous hydroxyl loss (-OH) is observed up to 900° C. Due to disagreement concerning the nature of metakaolin, research has led to general consensus that metakaolin is not a simple mixture of amorphous silica (SiO2) and alumina (Al2O3), but rather a complex amorphous structure that retains some longer-range order (but not strictly crystalline) due to stacking of its hexagonal layers. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Between 100-200° C, clay minerals lose most of their adsorbed water. Between 500-800° C kaolinite becomes calcined by losing water through dehydroxilization. At this temperature range, kaolinite becomes metakaolin, with a two-dimensional order in crystal structure. In order to produce a pozzolan nearly complete dehydroxilization must be reached without overheating. This produces an amorphous, highly pozzolanic state, whereas overheating can cause sintering, to form the dead burnt, nonreactive refractory, called mullite.<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>Uses</b><BR> <EOL>Calcined kaolin clay is used as a functional extender in paint. For example, calcined kaolin clay has proven to be an excellent extender for titanium dioxide (white) pigment in paint. This is because kaolin clay is chemically inert, has a high covering power, gives desirable flow properties and reduces the amount of expensive pigments required. Its hardness also improves physical durability of the paint film and its burnish resistance. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Kaolin clay is also used in grounds, such as for painting and for gilding. The kaolin clay can be used in recipes calling for ""pipe clay"" and mixed with starch or flour to make a thick cream and applied to wood panel or canvas supports for painting. The ground dries quickly and several very thin layers applied one after another to form a ground typical of 19th century paintings. <EOL>",,1000000,6,N,3.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8681,"Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Grounds/Terra Alba, Vicenza Earth & White Kaolinite with Bags",,9.620,,Saturday 13 November 2010 11:00:31 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,6.850,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
54742,NAP-510-15KLN5K,rommel,White Kaolinite 5 kg (11 lbs) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,White Kaolinite 5 kg (11 lbs) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,11,27.500,27.500,,"White Kaolinite 5 kg (11 lbs) Bag<BR><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><BR> <EOL><b>Physical Properties</b><BR> <EOL>* Median Particle Size (microns): 1.5<br> <EOL>* Hegman Grind: 5.5<br> <EOL>* Residue 325 Mesh (%) (ASTM C 325-81 or C 371-77): 0.05<br> <EOL>* Specific Gravity (ASTM C-329-75): 2.58<br><br> <EOL><b>Bulk Density:</b><br> <EOL>* Loose (lbs/cu ft): 23<br> <EOL>* Compacted (lbs/cu ft): 33<br> <EOL>* Mohs Hardness: 2.0-2.5<br> <EOL>* Oil Absorption (Gardner-Coleman): 60 g<br> <EOL>* pH Value (ASTM D 1208-78): 6.0<br> <EOL>* Brightness (Colorimeter): 	89<bR> <EOL>* Color: White<br> <EOL>* Refractive Index: 1.62<br> <EOL>* Moisture Content (max. %) (ASTM C 323-56 or C 234-82): 0.4<br> <EOL>* Loss on Ignition (%) (ASTM C 323-56): 0.3<br><br> <EOL><b>Chemical Analysis</b><br> <EOL>* Chemical Formula: Al<sub>2</sub>Si<sub>2</sub>O<sub>5</sub>(OH)<sub>4</sub><br> <EOL>* Silicon Dioxide (SiO<sub>2</sub>): 57.00%<br> <EOL>* Aluminum Oxide (Al<sub>2</sub>OS<ub>3</sub>): 39.00%<br> <EOL>* Iron Oxide (Fe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>): 1.00%<br> <EOL>* Titanium Dioxide (TiO<sub>2</sub>): 0.70%<br> <EOL>* Calcium Oxide (CaO) + Magnesium Oxide (MgO): 0.35%<br> <EOL>* Potassium Oxide (K<sub>2</sub>O) + Sodium Oxide (Na<sub>2</sub>O): 1.70%<br><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Kaolinite </b><br> <EOL>Kaolinite is a clay mineral with the chemical composition Al<sub>2</sub>Si<sub>2</sub>O<sub>5</sub>(OH)<sub>4</sub>. It is a layered silicate mineral, also known as china clay or kaolin. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL><b>Source</b><BR> <EOL>The name is derived from Gaoling or Kao-Ling (""High Hill"") in Jingdezhen, Jiangxi province, China. Kaolinite was first described as a mineral species in 1867 for an occurrence in the Jari River basin of Brazil. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>Kaolinite is one of the most common minerals on earth. It is mined, as kaolin, in Brazil, France, United Kingdom, Germany, India, Australia, Korea, the People's Republic of China and the USA. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Kaolinite is a soft, earthy, usually white mineral, produced by the chemical weathering of aluminum silicate minerals like feldspar. In many parts of the world, it is colored pink-orange-red by iron oxide, giving it a distinct rust hue. Lighter concentrations of iron oxide yield white, yellow or light orange colors. Alternating layers of colored clay are sometimes found, as at Providence Canyon State Park in Georgia, USA. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Our white kaolin clay is from deposits in Texas, USA and is heat treated to remove some portion of its hydroxyl (OH) composition. Calcined kaolin is produced by heating ultrafine natural kaolinite to high temperatures in a kiln. The calcination process increases whiteness and hardness and alters the size and shape of the kaolin particles. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Kaolin-type clays undergo a series of transformations upon heating in air at atmospheric pressure. Dehydration begins at 550-600° C to produce disordered metakaolin, Al2Si2O7, but continuous hydroxyl loss (-OH) is observed up to 900° C. Due to disagreement concerning the nature of metakaolin, research has led to general consensus that metakaolin is not a simple mixture of amorphous silica (SiO2) and alumina (Al2O3), but rather a complex amorphous structure that retains some longer-range order (but not strictly crystalline) due to stacking of its hexagonal layers. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Between 100-200° C, clay minerals lose most of their adsorbed water. Between 500-800° C kaolinite becomes calcined by losing water through dehydroxilization. At this temperature range, kaolinite becomes metakaolin, with a two-dimensional order in crystal structure. In order to produce a pozzolan nearly complete dehydroxilization must be reached without overheating. This produces an amorphous, highly pozzolanic state, whereas overheating can cause sintering, to form the dead burnt, nonreactive refractory, called mullite.<bR><BR> <EOL> <EOL><b>Uses</b><BR> <EOL>Calcined kaolin clay is used as a functional extender in paint. For example, calcined kaolin clay has proven to be an excellent extender for titanium dioxide (white) pigment in paint. This is because kaolin clay is chemically inert, has a high covering power, gives desirable flow properties and reduces the amount of expensive pigments required. Its hardness also improves physical durability of the paint film and its burnish resistance. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Kaolin clay is also used in grounds, such as for painting and for gilding. The kaolin clay can be used in recipes calling for ""pipe clay"" and mixed with starch or flour to make a thick cream and applied to wood panel or canvas supports for painting. The ground dries quickly and several very thin layers applied one after another to form a ground typical of 19th century paintings. <EOL>",,1000000,16,N,9.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8681,"Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Grounds/Terra Alba, Vicenza Earth & White Kaolinite with Bags",,26.870,,Saturday 13 November 2010 11:14:06 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,27.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
