55308,NAP-530-41008,bhavesh,Wilson's Medium 8 oz (236 ml) Can: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Wilson's Medium 8 oz (236 ml) Can: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,0.500,25.350,25.350,,"Wilson's Medium 8 oz (236 ml) Can<BR><br> <EOL><b>About Wilson's Medium</b><Br> <EOL>Wilson's Medium is a clear, gel-like oil based on the 18th century oil painting medium of thickened linseed oil, turpentine and beeswax used by the English landscape painter, Richard Wilson (1 August 1714 – 15 May 1782), who may fairly claim the honor of being 'the father of British landscape painting,' and, according to George Field, also used by Joshua Reynolds. We've taken the original formula and improved upon it by using the palest bodied linseed oil, pure distilled gum spirits of turpentine and rheological castor wax instead of beeswax. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>Castor wax is obtained by the controlled hydrogenation of natural castor oil. When molten it is clear, transparent and largely colorless. Castor wax is practically odorless and has the same toxicity as linseed oil or other vegetable oils. Castor wax is extremely hard in comparison with most other waxes, so it can be used in much smaller amounts than beeswax to provide the same properties. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL><B>Suggested Uses</b><BR> <EOL><B>Mix Directly with Oil Paints.</b> No driers or resins are added to Wilson's Medium, so it can be safely added to oil paints. Mix it directly with colors to give oil paint a buttery consistency that holds brushstrokes yet dries to satin finish. <EOL><br><BR> <EOL><b>Use to Make Oil Paint.</b> Add Wilson's Medium to pigment and oil when making your own paint. Paints often need the addition of rheological additives to prevent the settling of pigments during long periods of storage and to impart certain behavioral characteristics, such as to prevent slumping. Wilson's Medium changes the viscosity of paint by thickening it and imparts rheological properties, such as shear thinning (thixotropy). <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL><b>Use to 'Oil Out' or as a Painting Couch.</b> Wipe a thin coat of Wilson's Medium onto the surface of the dried paint just before painting a fresh layer. Wilson's Medium restores the dried, matte appearance of paint to a fresh appearance, without making it glossy.",,999999,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8737,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Vehicles & Mediums/Mix Mediums,,22.850,,Wednesday 17 November 2010 08:59:50 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,19.010,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58441,NAP-630-BKTW04,bhavesh,Wire Stand 6-inch,Wire Stand 6-inch,0.100,5.950,5.950,,<B>Wire Stand 6-inch</b><BR><BR> <EOL><B>About Wire Stand</b><BR> <EOL>Ideal for use while painting and for display. This small metal wire stand will support your painting panel (up to 9.5 by 12.5 in.) in an upright position (appox. 30 degrees from vertical) while painting and after it is completed for display.,,1000000,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8932,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Tools,,8.090,,Saturday 11 December 2010 10:23:56 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,5.950,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
58551,NAP-681-14512,bhavesh,Wood Float: 12" x 3 1/2",Wood Float: 12" x 3 1/2",0.500,4.500,4.500,,"<B>Wood Float: 12"" x 3 1/2""</b><BR><BR> <EOL><b>About Wood Float</b><BR> <EOL>Floats are used to assist in preparing the surface for troweling, or if a float (rough) finish is desired, floating is the final operation. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>This wood float is made from 1.27 cm (1/2 in.) thick seasoned mahogany with a very smooth finish. The plastic handle is both comfortable and durable. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL>Floats are made of aluminum, magnesium, wood, cork and rubber. The most popular float for fresco is wood. The best selling sizes in wood are 30.5 X 12.7 cm (12 X 5 inches).",,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8932,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Tools,,6.120,,Monday 13 December 2010 06:48:15 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,4.500,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55259,NAP-510-53DXT1K,bhavesh,Yellow Dextrin 1 kg (2.2 lb) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Yellow Dextrin 1 kg (2.2 lb) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,2.200,8.900,8.900,,"Yellow Dextrin 1 kg (2.2 lb) Bag<BR><br> <EOL><b>About Dextrin</b><Br> <EOL>Dextrin is processed starch used as a binder in combination with (or in place of) gum arabic. It thickens paint, altering a taffy-like vehicle to a smooth, buttery consistency, and reduces surface gloss or bronzing in the dried color. Watercolors can be given a ""short"" or stiff consistency with dextrin.",,1000000,3,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,9.080,,Wednesday 17 November 2010 07:38:21 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,6.680,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55265,NAP-510-53DXT04,bhavesh,Yellow Dextrin 4 oz (118.3 cc) Jar: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Yellow Dextrin 4 oz (118.3 cc) Jar: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,0.250,4.500,4.500,,"Yellow Dextrin 4 oz (118.3 cc) Jar<BR><br> <EOL><b>About Dextrin</b><Br> <EOL>Dextrin is processed starch used as a binder in combination with (or in place of) gum arabic. It thickens paint, altering a taffy-like vehicle to a smooth, buttery consistency, and reduces surface gloss or bronzing in the dried color. Watercolors can be given a ""short"" or stiff consistency with dextrin.",,1000000,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8459,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments,,4.600,,Wednesday 17 November 2010 07:48:15 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,3.380,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55264,NAP-510-53DXT50,bhavesh,Yellow Dextrin 500g (1 lb) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Yellow Dextrin 500g (1 lb) Bag: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,1.100,6.850,6.850,,"Yellow Dextrin 454 g (1 lb) Bag<BR><br> <EOL><b>About Dextrin</b><Br> <EOL>Dextrin is processed starch used as a binder in combination with (or in place of) gum arabic. It thickens paint, altering a taffy-like vehicle to a smooth, buttery consistency, and reduces surface gloss or bronzing in the dried color. Watercolors can be given a ""short"" or stiff consistency with dextrin.",,1000000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8729,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Vehicles & Mediums/Yellow Dextrins,,6.990,,Wednesday 17 November 2010 07:45:49 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,5.140,0,N,33,Natural Pigments
55009,NAP-500-ZRDR02,bhavesh,Zirconium Drier (2 oz) Bottle: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,Zirconium Drier (2 oz) Bottle: Made in USA by Natural Pigments,0.130,8.250,8.250,,"Zirconium Drier (2 oz) Bottle<BR><br> <EOL><b>Specifications</b><Br> <EOL>* Appearance: Light yellow liquid<bR> <EOL>* Color (Gardner): 4<br> <EOL>* Zirconium Content (% weight): 12<br> <EOL>* Non Volatile Content (% weight): 42<br> <EOL>* Specific Gravity (@25 ° C., kg/L): 1.255<br> <EOL>* Viscosity (@25 ° C., Gardner): H<bR><bR> <EOL> <EOL><b>About Zirconium Drier</b><BR> <EOL>Zirconium Drier is a concentrated blend of metal carboxylates in mineral spirits, containing 12% zirconium and 5% calcium. Use with cobalt or manganese driers to improve through-dry and as a replacement for lead driers. <EOL><bR><BR> <EOL>Zirconium and calcium are effective auxiliary driers when used in conjunction with active driers, such as cobalt or manganese. Use Zirconium Drier to promote the through drying of paint film. Zirconium is the most effective replacement for lead driers. It also improves gloss and color when substituted for lead. Calcium functions as a pigment wetting agent to improve dispersion of pigments in oil and alkyd vehicles thereby improving gloss and hardness of paint. When ground with pigments it minimizes loss of drying capability of other driers. It improves the action of cobalt driers and is used in conjunction with them and assists in the ""through dry"" of oil and alkyd paint. <EOL><Br><BR> <EOL>Typically, 0.1% to 0.3% of zirconium metal is added to oil and alkyd paint based on the weight of the binder. Even higher levels may be required for high solids alkyd paint (low in volatile solvents). <EOL><br><BR> <EOL>The dropper bottle makes dispensing easy. Add one drop per 5 ml (about 1 teaspoon) of paint. Suggested use levels should be verified with tests. <EOL><BR><BR> <EOL><b>Label Information</b><BR> <EOL><b>CONTAINS: PETROLEUM DISTILLATES.</b><BR> Exposure may cause skin and eye irritation. Overexposure will cause dizziness, drowsiness, headache, nausea and cracking or drying of skin. Avoid contact with skin. Avoid breathing mist or vapor. Wear safety glasses, protective clothing and chemical resistant rubber gloves when handling. Wash thoroughly after handling. Do not take internally.<br><br> <EOL> <EOL><b>Eye Contact:</b><BR> <EOL>Flush eyes at once with large amounts of water for at least 15 minutes, while holding lids open. Get medical attention.<bR><br> <EOL><b>Skin Contact:</b><BR> <EOL>Wash thoroughly with soap and water. Wash clothes and shoes before reuse. If symptoms occur, get medical attention.<bR><BR> <EOL><b>Inhalation:</b><Br> <EOL> Remove to fresh air.<br><BR> <EOL><b>Ingestion:</b><BR> <EOL> Seek medical attention.",,999999,1,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,8736,Uncategorized/Natural Pigments/Vehicles & Mediums/Drieres,,8.420,,Tuesday 16 November 2010 05:27:11 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,282,,6.190,0,N,33,Natural Pigments

